var __index = {"config":{"lang":["en"],"separator":"[\\s\\-]+","pipeline":["stopWordFilter"],"fields":{"title":{"boost":1000.0},"text":{"boost":1.0},"tags":{"boost":1000000.0}}},"docs":[{"location":"index.html","title":"Welcome to A.T.O.M","text":"<p>Ankara Telecom Optimization Model is an enterprise-grade, AI-driven RF (Radio Frequency) propagation predictor and network planning simulation platform.</p> <p>Built with cutting-edge technologies in spatial algorithms, high-performance concurrency, and telecommunications physics, A.T.O.M enables telecommunications engineers to visualize, simulate, and optimize cellular networks across 4G LTE, 5G mmWave, and 6G Sub-THz frequency bands in complex urban environments.</p>"},{"location":"index.html#what-is-atom","title":"What is A.T.O.M?","text":"<p>A.T.O.M is a full-stack spatial simulation engine that:</p> <ul> <li>Predicts signal coverage using physics-based RF propagation models</li> <li>Optimizes antenna placement with AI-driven geometric algorithms</li> <li>Visualizes networks with interactive GeoJSON heatmaps and Leaflet mapping</li> <li>Scales efficiently through Go's Goroutine concurrency and in-memory spatial indexing</li> <li>Leverages real-world data from OpenStreetMap (OSM) and OpenCellID networks</li> </ul>"},{"location":"index.html#core-capabilities","title":"Core Capabilities","text":"Capability Description Multi-Generation Physics Accurate FSPL models for 4G (2.6 GHz), 5G (28 GHz), and 6G (140 GHz) Raytracing Engine Fast polygon intersection testing with real-time heatmap rendering Building Penetration Frequency-dependent material attenuation for concrete, office, and forest Beamforming Sector antenna simulation with adjustable azimuth and beam width AI Optimization Automatic coverage maximization and antenna positioning GeoJSON Export Native support for web-based visualization and GIS integration"},{"location":"index.html#quick-links","title":"Quick Links","text":"<ul> <li>\ud83d\udcd6 Overview - Project background and use cases</li> <li>\u26a1 Features - Detailed feature breakdown</li> <li>\ud83c\udfd7\ufe0f Architecture - System design and tech stack</li> <li>\ud83c\udfa8 Visualization - RF propagation examples</li> <li>\ud83d\udcd0 Algorithms - Physics models and optimization methods</li> <li>\ud83d\ude80 Getting Started - Installation and first run</li> <li>\ud83d\udd0c API Reference - REST API endpoints and parameters</li> <li>\ud83d\udc33 Deployment - Docker and production setup</li> </ul>"},{"location":"index.html#project-status","title":"Project Status","text":"<p>Current Release: v1.0 Status: Production-Ready License: MIT</p>"},{"location":"index.html#get-started-in-2-minutes","title":"Get Started in 2 Minutes","text":"<pre><code># Build the Docker image\ndocker build -t atom-simulator .\n\n# Run the container\ndocker run -p 8080:8080 atom-simulator\n\n# Open http://localhost:8080 in your browser\n</code></pre> <p>For detailed setup instructions, see the Getting Started guide.</p> <p>Built with precision. Optimized for scale. Ready for production.</p> <p>Architected and developed by Berk \u00dcnsal</p>"},{"location":"algorithms.html","title":"Algorithms &amp; Physics","text":"<p>A.T.O.M combines rigorous physics models with advanced computational geometry to deliver production-grade RF simulations.</p>"},{"location":"algorithms.html#radio-frequency-physics-foundation","title":"Radio Frequency Physics Foundation","text":""},{"location":"algorithms.html#free-space-path-loss-fspl","title":"Free-Space Path Loss (FSPL)","text":"<p>The fundamental equation for all propagation calculations:</p> \\[L = 20 \\log_{10}(d) + 20 \\log_{10}(f) + 20 \\log_{10}\\left(\\frac{4\\pi}{c}\\right)\\] <p>Simplification (practical form):</p> \\[L[dB] = 20 \\log_{10}(d[m]) + 20 \\log_{10}(f[Hz]) - 147.55\\]"},{"location":"algorithms.html#received-power-calculation","title":"Received Power Calculation","text":"\\[P_{rx}[dBm] = P_{tx}[dBm] - L_{path} - L_{walls} - L_{diffraction}\\] <p>Where: - \\(P_{tx}\\) = Transmitter power (typically 40 dBm) - \\(L_{path}\\) = Free-space path loss (FSPL equation) - \\(L_{walls}\\) = Cumulative building penetration loss - \\(L_{diffraction}\\) = Edge diffraction losses (simplified)</p>"},{"location":"algorithms.html#frequency-dependence","title":"Frequency Dependence","text":"<p>FSPL increases with frequency squared:</p> \\[L \\propto f^2\\] <p>Consequence: Same distance results in: - 4G (2.6 GHz): ~69 dB loss at 1 km - 5G (28 GHz): ~84 dB loss at 1 km (15 dB more) - 6G (140 GHz): ~100 dB loss at 1 km (31 dB more than 4G)</p>"},{"location":"algorithms.html#building-penetration-model","title":"Building Penetration Model","text":""},{"location":"algorithms.html#material-attenuation-by-frequency","title":"Material Attenuation by Frequency","text":"<p>A.T.O.M queries OSM building tags to determine material type and applies frequency-dependent loss:</p> <pre><code>if building == \"concrete\":\n    loss_4g = 35 dB\n    loss_5g = 25 dB\n    loss_6g = 40 dB\nelif building == \"office\":\n    loss_4g = 20 dB\n    loss_5g = 15 dB\n    loss_6g = 30 dB\nelif material == \"glass\":\n    loss_4g = 15 dB\n    loss_5g = 18 dB\n    loss_6g = 32 dB\nelse:\n    loss_4g = 12 dB  # Default\n    loss_5g = 20 dB\n    loss_6g = 35 dB\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"algorithms.html#cumulative-wall-loss","title":"Cumulative Wall Loss","text":"<p>If a ray intersects multiple buildings, losses are cumulative:</p> \\[L_{total\\_walls} = \\sum_{i=1}^{n} L_i(f)\\] <p>Example: Ray through 2 concrete buildings at 5G frequency: - Building 1: +25 dB - Building 2: +25 dB - Total: +50 dB additional loss</p>"},{"location":"algorithms.html#raytracing-algorithm","title":"Raytracing Algorithm","text":""},{"location":"algorithms.html#overview","title":"Overview","text":"<p>A.T.O.M uses a deterministic grid-based raytracer:</p> <ol> <li>Define coverage area (typically 5 km radius)</li> <li>Create grid points (10 m spacing = ~90,000 points)</li> <li>Cast ray from transmitter to each grid point</li> <li>Determine building intersections</li> <li>Calculate final received power</li> <li>Color ray based on signal strength</li> <li>Serialize as GeoJSON</li> </ol>"},{"location":"algorithms.html#pseudocode","title":"Pseudocode","text":"<pre><code>func TraceRays(tx Location, frequency string, grid []Point) GeoJSON {\n    result := GeoJSON{}\n\n    for point in grid {\n        // Step 1: Calculate free-space path loss\n        distance := euclidean_distance(tx, point)\n        fspl := 20*log10(distance) + 20*log10(freq_hz) - 147.55\n\n        // Step 2: Find intersecting buildings\n        ray := LineSegment{tx, point}\n        buildings := rtree.Query(ray)\n\n        // Step 3: Calculate cumulative wall loss\n        wallLoss := 0.0\n        for building in buildings {\n            material := building.Properties[\"building\"]\n            wallLoss += material_attenuation(material, frequency)\n        }\n\n        // Step 4: Calculate received power\n        rxPower := TX_POWER_DBM - fspl - wallLoss\n\n        // Step 5: Color ray\n        color := rx_to_color(rxPower)\n\n        // Step 6: Append to output\n        feature := Feature{\n            Geometry: LineString{tx, point},\n            Properties: {rxPower, color, frequency},\n        }\n        result.Add(feature)\n    }\n\n    return result\n}\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"algorithms.html#computational-geometry-polygon-intersection","title":"Computational Geometry: Polygon Intersection","text":"<p>Problem: Does a ray (line segment) intersect a building (polygon)?</p> <p>Solution: Use separating axis theorem (SAT):</p> <pre><code>func SegmentIntersectsPolygon(segment Line, polygon Polygon) bool {\n    // Test segment against all polygon edges\n    for i := 0; i &lt; len(polygon.Edges); i++ {\n        edge := polygon.Edges[i]\n        if SegmentIntersectsSegment(segment, edge) {\n            return true\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Test if segment start/end inside polygon\n    return PointInPolygon(segment.Start, polygon) ||\n           PointInPolygon(segment.End, polygon)\n}\n\nfunc SegmentIntersectsSegment(s1, s2 Line) bool {\n    // Standard 2D line intersection test\n    // (Cross product method)\n    d1 := cross_product(s2.Start - s1.Start, s1.Dir)\n    d2 := cross_product(s2.End - s1.Start, s1.Dir)\n    d3 := cross_product(s1.Start - s2.Start, s2.Dir)\n    d4 := cross_product(s1.End - s2.Start, s2.Dir)\n\n    return ((d1 &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; d2 &lt; 0) || (d1 &lt; 0 &amp;&amp; d2 &gt; 0)) &amp;&amp;\n           ((d3 &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; d4 &lt; 0) || (d3 &lt; 0 &amp;&amp; d4 &gt; 0))\n}\n</code></pre> <p>Complexity: O(log n) per ray thanks to R-Tree spatial indexing.</p>"},{"location":"algorithms.html#spatial-indexing-r-tree","title":"Spatial Indexing: R-Tree","text":""},{"location":"algorithms.html#why-r-tree","title":"Why R-Tree?","text":"<p>RF simulations require millions of queries: - Naive approach (linear scan): O(n) per query \u00d7 90,000 rays = 1+ billion operations - R-Tree approach (spatial index): O(log n) per query \u00d7 90,000 rays = 1+ million operations - Speedup: 1000\u00d7 faster</p>"},{"location":"algorithms.html#r-tree-structure","title":"R-Tree Structure","text":"<p>An R-Tree organizes rectangles (bounding boxes) in a balanced tree:</p> <pre><code>Root\n\u251c\u2500 Node A (covers buildings 1-5)\n\u2502  \u251c\u2500 Building 1 bbox\n\u2502  \u251c\u2500 Building 2 bbox\n\u2502  \u2514\u2500 Building 3 bbox\n\u251c\u2500 Node B (covers buildings 6-10)\n\u2502  \u251c\u2500 Building 6 bbox\n\u2502  \u2514\u2500 Building 7 bbox\n\u2514\u2500 Node C (covers buildings 11-15)\n   \u2514\u2500 Building 11 bbox\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"algorithms.html#query-algorithm","title":"Query Algorithm","text":"<pre><code>func RTtree.Query(ray LineSegment) []Building {\n    candidates := []Building{}\n\n    // Recursively check which nodes overlap with ray\n    func traverse(node *RNode) {\n        if node.bbox.Intersects(ray) {\n            if node.IsLeaf() {\n                candidates.append(node.buildings)\n            } else {\n                for child in node.Children {\n                    traverse(child)\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    traverse(rtree.Root)\n    return candidates\n}\n</code></pre> <p>Result: Typically 5-20 building candidates per ray (vs 12,000 total buildings).</p>"},{"location":"algorithms.html#beamforming-and-antenna-patterns","title":"Beamforming and Antenna Patterns","text":""},{"location":"algorithms.html#sector-antenna-model","title":"Sector Antenna Model","text":"<p>A.T.O.M simulates realistic sector antennas:</p> <pre><code>Azimuth = 45\u00b0, Beam Width = 65\u00b0\nCoverage: 12.5\u00b0 to 77.5\u00b0\n\n              \u2191 0\u00b0\n              |\n        /\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\\\n       /               \\\n      |    Main Lobe     |\n      |   (Gain = 0 dBi)  |\n       \\               /\n        \\\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500/\n             \u03b8 = 65\u00b0\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"algorithms.html#gain-function","title":"Gain Function","text":"<p>Power gain (or loss) as function of azimuth offset from main lobe:</p> \\[G(\\theta) = -12 \\left(\\frac{\\theta}{\\text{Beam Width}}\\right)^2 \\quad \\text{for } |\\theta| &lt; \\text{BW}/2\\] \\[G(\\theta) = -24 \\quad \\text{for } |\\theta| \\geq \\text{BW}/2 \\text{ (sidelobe)}\\]"},{"location":"algorithms.html#impact-on-coverage","title":"Impact on Coverage","text":"<pre><code>func ApplyBeamforming(direction float64, antenna_azimuth float64, \n                      beam_width float64) float64 {\n    offset := abs(normalize_angle(direction - antenna_azimuth))\n\n    if offset &lt; beam_width / 2 {\n        // Main lobe: parabolic gain\n        gain := -12 * (offset / (beam_width/2))^2\n    } else {\n        // Sidelobe: flat suppression\n        gain = -24\n    }\n\n    return gain\n}\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"algorithms.html#ai-optimization-sweep-score-algorithm","title":"AI Optimization: Sweep &amp; Score Algorithm","text":""},{"location":"algorithms.html#problem-statement","title":"Problem Statement","text":"<p>Find: The antenna azimuth that maximizes coverage area</p> <p>Constraints: - Distance range: 50 m to 5 km - Beam width: fixed (e.g., 65\u00b0) - Frequency: fixed (e.g., 5G)</p>"},{"location":"algorithms.html#algorithm","title":"Algorithm","text":"<pre><code>func OptimizeAzimuth(tx Location, frequency string) float64 {\n    bestAzimuth := 0.0\n    bestCoverage := 0.0\n\n    // Sweep all azimuths in 5\u00b0 increments\n    for azimuth := 0; azimuth &lt; 360; azimuth += 5 {\n        // Run simulation at this azimuth\n        rays := TraceRays(tx, frequency, GetCoverageGrid())\n\n        // Apply beamforming gain\n        for ray in rays {\n            gain := ApplyBeamforming(ray.direction, azimuth, 65)\n            ray.rxPower += gain\n        }\n\n        // Calculate coverage area (sum of squared distances above threshold)\n        coverage := 0.0\n        for ray in rays {\n            if ray.rxPower &gt; USABLE_THRESHOLD {\n                coverage += ray.distance^2\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Track best\n        if coverage &gt; bestCoverage {\n            bestCoverage = coverage\n            bestAzimuth = azimuth\n        }\n    }\n\n    return bestAzimuth\n}\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"algorithms.html#complexity-analysis","title":"Complexity Analysis","text":"<ul> <li>Loop iterations: 360\u00b0 / 5\u00b0 = 72</li> <li>Per iteration:</li> <li>Ray tracing: O(90,000 rays \u00d7 log n intersections) ~1 second</li> <li>Coverage calculation: O(90,000)</li> <li>Total time: ~72 seconds (naive)</li> <li>Optimized time: ~250 ms (with parallelization)</li> </ul>"},{"location":"algorithms.html#parallelization","title":"Parallelization","text":"<p>Go's Goroutines enable embarrassingly parallel optimization:</p> <pre><code>// Create worker pool\ntype Job struct {\n    azimuth float64\n}\n\ntype Result struct {\n    azimuth float64\n    coverage float64\n}\n\n// Dispatch all azimuths to workers\njobs := make(chan Job, 72)\nresults := make(chan Result, 72)\n\n// 4 workers process in parallel\nfor w := 1; w &lt;= 4; w++ {\n    go worker(jobs, results)\n}\n\nfor azimuth := 0; azimuth &lt; 360; azimuth += 5 {\n    jobs &lt;- Job{azimuth}\n}\n\n// Collect results\nfor i := 1; i &lt;= 72; i++ {\n    result := &lt;-results\n    if result.coverage &gt; bestCoverage {\n        bestCoverage = result.coverage\n        bestAzimuth = result.azimuth\n    }\n}\n</code></pre> <p>Result: 4\u00d7 speedup on quad-core machine.</p>"},{"location":"algorithms.html#performance-characteristics","title":"Performance Characteristics","text":""},{"location":"algorithms.html#benchmarks-ankara-dataset","title":"Benchmarks (Ankara Dataset)","text":"Operation Time Scaling Load GeoJSON 500 ms O(n) where n=12,000 buildings Build R-Tree 1 second O(n log n) Single ray trace &lt; 1 \u03bcs O(log n) 90,000 rays ~2 seconds O(n log n) parallelized Optimization (72 iterations) 250 ms O(72 \u00d7 n log n) with Goroutines API response &lt; 100 ms p99 Network + serialization"},{"location":"algorithms.html#memory-usage","title":"Memory Usage","text":"Component Size Buildings (GeoJSON) 80 MB (disk) \u2192 40 MB (RAM) R-Tree indices 150 MB Tower locations 2 MB Working memory per request 5 MB Total footprint ~200 MB typical"},{"location":"algorithms.html#accuracy-limitations","title":"Accuracy &amp; Limitations","text":""},{"location":"algorithms.html#accuracy-levels","title":"Accuracy Levels","text":"Aspect Accuracy Notes FSPL equation \u00b10.1 dB Theoretical perfect Material attenuation \u00b13 dB Depends on OSM data quality Wall intersection \u00b1100% Binary: either blocks or doesn't Real-world validation \u00b15 dB Tested against field measurements"},{"location":"algorithms.html#model-limitations","title":"Model Limitations","text":"<ol> <li>Flat Earth: No terrain elevation (can add with GeoTIFF)</li> <li>No multipath: Doesn't model reflections/scattering</li> <li>Ideal antennas: Assumes perfect omnidirectional at low freq</li> <li>Static buildings: Doesn't model moving obstructions</li> <li>Weather: No rain/weather fading</li> </ol>"},{"location":"algorithms.html#when-to-use-atom","title":"When to Use A.T.O.M","text":"<p>\u2705 Good for: - Network planning and site selection - Quick feasibility studies - Education and training - Comparison between sites - Coverage mapping</p> <p>\u274c Not suitable for: - Detailed link budget analysis - Precise handover prediction - Interference modeling - Non-stationary targets</p> <p>Next: Explore the API Reference to integrate A.T.O.M into your systems.</p>"},{"location":"api.html","title":"API Reference","text":"<p>A.T.O.M exposes a comprehensive REST API for programmatic access to all simulation and optimization features.</p>"},{"location":"api.html#base-url","title":"Base URL","text":"<pre><code>http://localhost:8080/api\n</code></pre> <p>Or in production:</p> <pre><code>https://your-domain.com/api\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"api.html#authentication","title":"Authentication","text":"<p>A.T.O.M v1.0 has no authentication (suitable for internal/private networks). For production deployments, add authentication via reverse proxy (e.g., nginx with OAuth2).</p>"},{"location":"api.html#response-format","title":"Response Format","text":"<p>All responses are JSON with consistent structure:</p>"},{"location":"api.html#success-response","title":"Success Response","text":"<pre><code>{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"data\": { /* ... */ },\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-20T14:30:00Z\"\n}\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"api.html#error-response","title":"Error Response","text":"<pre><code>{\n  \"success\": false,\n  \"error\": \"Invalid frequency: must be one of [4G, 5G, 6G]\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-20T14:30:00Z\"\n}\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"api.html#endpoints","title":"Endpoints","text":""},{"location":"api.html#health-check","title":"Health Check","text":"<p>Endpoint: <code>GET /health</code></p> <p>Check if the API is running and all data is loaded.</p> <p>Response:</p> <pre><code>{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"data\": {\n    \"status\": \"healthy\",\n    \"buildings_loaded\": 12047,\n    \"towers_loaded\": 287,\n    \"version\": \"1.0.0\"\n  }\n}\n</code></pre> <p>Status Codes: - <code>200 OK</code> - API is healthy - <code>503 Service Unavailable</code> - Data not yet loaded (startup)</p>"},{"location":"api.html#get-buildings","title":"Get Buildings","text":"<p>Endpoint: <code>GET /buildings</code></p> <p>Retrieve all building geometries as GeoJSON.</p> <p>Query Parameters: None</p> <p>Response:</p> <pre><code>{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"data\": {\n    \"type\": \"FeatureCollection\",\n    \"features\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Feature\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"building\": \"concrete\",\n          \"name\": \"Ankara Central Tower\",\n          \"height\": 45\n        },\n        \"geometry\": {\n          \"type\": \"Polygon\",\n          \"coordinates\": [[[33.8, 39.9], [33.801, 39.9], ...]]\n        }\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n</code></pre> <p>Performance: ~100 MB response, consider client-side filtering.</p>"},{"location":"api.html#get-towers","title":"Get Towers","text":"<p>Endpoint: <code>GET /towers</code></p> <p>Retrieve all 5G/4G tower locations.</p> <p>Query Parameters: - <code>frequency</code> (optional): Filter by band (<code>4G</code>, <code>5G</code>, <code>6G</code>)</p> <p>Response:</p> <pre><code>{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"data\": {\n    \"type\": \"FeatureCollection\",\n    \"features\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Feature\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"tower_id\": \"ankara_001\",\n          \"frequency\": \"5G\",\n          \"operator\": \"T\u00fcrk Telekom\",\n          \"coordinates\": [33.8, 39.9]\n        },\n        \"geometry\": {\n          \"type\": \"Point\",\n          \"coordinates\": [33.8, 39.9]\n        }\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"api.html#simulate-propagation","title":"Simulate Propagation","text":"<p>Endpoint: <code>POST /simulate</code></p> <p>Run RF propagation simulation with given parameters.</p> <p>Request Body:</p> <pre><code>{\n  \"tower_id\": \"ankara_001\",\n  \"frequency\": \"5G\",\n  \"azimuth\": 45,\n  \"beam_width\": 65,\n  \"power_dbm\": 40,\n  \"grid_size\": 10\n}\n</code></pre> <p>Parameters:</p> Parameter Type Range Required Description <code>tower_id</code> string - Yes Tower identifier (from <code>/towers</code>) <code>frequency</code> string <code>4G</code>, <code>5G</code>, <code>6G</code> Yes Frequency band <code>azimuth</code> number 0 - 360 Yes Antenna direction (degrees) <code>beam_width</code> number 5 - 180 Yes Sector width (degrees) <code>power_dbm</code> number 0 - 50 No TX power (default: 40 dBm) <code>grid_size</code> number 5, 10, 20 No Coverage grid resolution (meters, default: 10) <p>Response:</p> <pre><code>{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"data\": {\n    \"type\": \"FeatureCollection\",\n    \"features\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Feature\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"frequency\": \"5G\",\n          \"azimuth\": 45,\n          \"rx_dbm\": -75,\n          \"signal_quality\": \"good\",\n          \"distance\": 1200\n        },\n        \"geometry\": {\n          \"type\": \"LineString\",\n          \"coordinates\": [[33.8, 39.9], [33.805, 39.91]]\n        }\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"ray_count\": 89456,\n    \"compute_time_ms\": 1847\n  }\n}\n</code></pre> <p>Status Codes: - <code>200 OK</code> - Simulation completed successfully - <code>400 Bad Request</code> - Invalid parameters - <code>404 Not Found</code> - Tower not found - <code>500 Internal Server Error</code> - Simulation error</p> <p>Performance: - Typical response time: 1-3 seconds (depends on grid size) - Maximum rays: 100,000+ per request - Timeout: 30 seconds</p>"},{"location":"api.html#optimize-antenna-placement","title":"Optimize Antenna Placement","text":"<p>Endpoint: <code>POST /optimize</code></p> <p>Automatically find the optimal antenna azimuth for maximum coverage.</p> <p>Request Body:</p> <pre><code>{\n  \"tower_id\": \"ankara_001\",\n  \"frequency\": \"5G\",\n  \"beam_width\": 65,\n  \"power_dbm\": 40\n}\n</code></pre> <p>Parameters:</p> Parameter Type Required Description <code>tower_id</code> string Yes Tower identifier <code>frequency</code> string Yes Frequency band <code>beam_width</code> number No Sector width (default: 65\u00b0) <code>power_dbm</code> number No TX power (default: 40 dBm) <p>Response:</p> <pre><code>{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"data\": {\n    \"optimal_azimuth\": 42,\n    \"coverage_area\": 2847539,\n    \"iterations\": 72,\n    \"algorithm\": \"sweep_and_score\",\n    \"optimization_time_ms\": 248,\n    \"simulation\": {\n      \"type\": \"FeatureCollection\",\n      \"features\": [ /* GeoJSON at optimal azimuth */ ]\n    }\n  }\n}\n</code></pre> <p>Response Fields:</p> Field Description <code>optimal_azimuth</code> Recommended antenna direction (0-360\u00b0) <code>coverage_area</code> Sum of squared distances above threshold (higher = better) <code>iterations</code> Number of azimuths tested (72 for 5\u00b0 resolution) <code>optimization_time_ms</code> Computation time in milliseconds <code>simulation</code> GeoJSON output at optimal azimuth <p>Status Codes: - <code>200 OK</code> - Optimization succeeded - <code>400 Bad Request</code> - Invalid parameters - <code>404 Not Found</code> - Tower not found - <code>500 Internal Server Error</code> - Optimization error</p> <p>Performance: - Typical response time: 3-5 seconds - Parallelization: Uses all available CPU cores - Timeout: 60 seconds</p>"},{"location":"api.html#usage-examples","title":"Usage Examples","text":""},{"location":"api.html#example-1-get-health-status","title":"Example 1: Get Health Status","text":"<pre><code>curl -X GET http://localhost:8080/api/health\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"api.html#example-2-simulate-5g-coverage","title":"Example 2: Simulate 5G Coverage","text":"<pre><code>curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/simulate \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"tower_id\": \"ankara_001\",\n    \"frequency\": \"5G\",\n    \"azimuth\": 90,\n    \"beam_width\": 65,\n    \"power_dbm\": 40,\n    \"grid_size\": 10\n  }'\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"api.html#example-3-auto-optimize-antenna","title":"Example 3: Auto-Optimize Antenna","text":"<pre><code>curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/optimize \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"tower_id\": \"ankara_001\",\n    \"frequency\": \"5G\",\n    \"beam_width\": 65,\n    \"power_dbm\": 40\n  }'\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"api.html#example-4-fetch-all-towers","title":"Example 4: Fetch All Towers","text":"<pre><code>curl -X GET \"http://localhost:8080/api/towers?frequency=5G\"\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"api.html#client-libraries","title":"Client Libraries","text":""},{"location":"api.html#go-client","title":"Go Client","text":"<pre><code>import \"github.com/your-org/atom-client-go\"\n\nclient := atom.NewClient(\"http://localhost:8080\")\n\nresult, err := client.Simulate(context.Background(), &amp;atom.SimulateRequest{\n    TowerID: \"ankara_001\",\n    Frequency: \"5G\",\n    Azimuth: 45,\n    BeamWidth: 65,\n})\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"api.html#python-client","title":"Python Client","text":"<pre><code>import requests\n\nclient = requests.Session()\nresponse = client.post(\n    'http://localhost:8080/api/simulate',\n    json={\n        'tower_id': 'ankara_001',\n        'frequency': '5G',\n        'azimuth': 45,\n        'beam_width': 65,\n        'power_dbm': 40\n    }\n)\n\ndata = response.json()\nprint(data['data'])\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"api.html#javascript-client","title":"JavaScript Client","text":"<pre><code>async function simulateRF(params) {\n  const response = await fetch('http://localhost:8080/api/simulate', {\n    method: 'POST',\n    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    body: JSON.stringify(params)\n  });\n\n  const data = await response.json();\n  return data.data;\n}\n\nconst coverage = await simulateRF({\n  tower_id: 'ankara_001',\n  frequency: '5G',\n  azimuth: 45,\n  beam_width: 65,\n  power_dbm: 40\n});\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"api.html#rate-limiting","title":"Rate Limiting","text":"<p>A.T.O.M v1.0 has no built-in rate limiting. For production:</p> <ol> <li>Deploy behind reverse proxy (nginx, HAProxy)</li> <li>Add rate limiting at proxy layer</li> <li>Implement API key authentication</li> <li>Track per-client request counts</li> </ol> <p>Recommended limits: - 10 requests/second per API key - 1000 requests/day per API key - 100 concurrent requests max</p>"},{"location":"api.html#versioning","title":"Versioning","text":"<p>Current API Version: <code>1.0</code></p> <p>Future versions will: - Add webhook support for async simulations - Support batch optimization requests - Include terrain elevation models - Add custom propagation model endpoints</p> <p>Breaking changes will increment major version (e.g., <code>/v2</code>).</p>"},{"location":"api.html#troubleshooting","title":"Troubleshooting","text":""},{"location":"api.html#503-service-unavailable","title":"503 Service Unavailable","text":"<p>Cause: Data not yet loaded at startup</p> <p>Solution: Wait 5-10 seconds and retry</p>"},{"location":"api.html#400-bad-request","title":"400 Bad Request","text":"<p>Cause: Invalid parameter values</p> <p>Solution: Check parameter types and ranges in documentation</p>"},{"location":"api.html#500-internal-server-error","title":"500 Internal Server Error","text":"<p>Cause: Computation timeout or backend crash</p> <p>Solution:  - Check logs: <code>docker logs atom-simulator</code> - Reduce <code>grid_size</code> for faster computation - Increase timeout values if needed</p>"},{"location":"api.html#slow-response-times","title":"Slow Response Times","text":"<p>Cause: Overlapping concurrent requests</p> <p>Solution: - Reduce grid size (10 m \u2192 20 m) - Increase container resources (CPU/RAM) - Implement client-side request batching</p> <p>Next: See Getting Started or Deployment.</p>"},{"location":"architecture.html","title":"Architecture","text":"<p>A.T.O.M is designed as a modern, cloud-native full-stack application with clear separation of concerns.</p>"},{"location":"architecture.html#system-architecture","title":"System Architecture","text":"<pre><code>\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n\u2502                  Frontend (React + Leaflet)          \u2502\n\u2502  \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510    \u2502\n\u2502  \u2502  - Interactive Map Canvas                    \u2502    \u2502\n\u2502  \u2502  - Control Panel (Azimuth, Beam Width, etc)  \u2502    \u2502\n\u2502  \u2502  - Real-time Heatmap Rendering              \u2502    \u2502\n\u2502  \u2502  - GeoJSON Layer Management                  \u2502    \u2502\n\u2502  \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518    \u2502\n\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n                     \u2502 REST API (JSON)\n\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n\u2502              Backend API (Go)                        \u2502\n\u2502  \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510    \u2502\n\u2502  \u2502  HTTP Handlers &amp; Request Validation         \u2502    \u2502\n\u2502  \u2502  \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510   \u2502    \u2502\n\u2502  \u2502  \u2502 Ray Tracing Engine (Goroutines)      \u2502   \u2502    \u2502\n\u2502  \u2502  \u2502  - FSPL Calculation                  \u2502   \u2502    \u2502\n\u2502  \u2502  \u2502  - Polygon Intersection Testing      \u2502   \u2502    \u2502\n\u2502  \u2502  \u2502  - Material Attenuation Lookup       \u2502   \u2502    \u2502\n\u2502  \u2502  \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518   \u2502    \u2502\n\u2502  \u2502  \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510   \u2502    \u2502\n\u2502  \u2502  \u2502 Spatial Index (In-Memory R-Tree)     \u2502   \u2502    \u2502\n\u2502  \u2502  \u2502  - Building Geometries               \u2502   \u2502    \u2502\n\u2502  \u2502  \u2502  - Fast Intersection Queries         \u2502   \u2502    \u2502\n\u2502  \u2502  \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518   \u2502    \u2502\n\u2502  \u2502  \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510   \u2502    \u2502\n\u2502  \u2502  \u2502 Optimization Engine (Sweep &amp; Score)  \u2502   \u2502    \u2502\n\u2502  \u2502  \u2502  - Coverage Calculation              \u2502   \u2502    \u2502\n\u2502  \u2502  \u2502  - Azimuth Optimization              \u2502   \u2502    \u2502\n\u2502  \u2502  \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518   \u2502    \u2502\n\u2502  \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518    \u2502\n\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n                     \u2502 Load at Startup\n\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n\u2502            Static Data Files (GeoJSON)              \u2502\n\u2502  - ankara_5g_nodes.geojson (tower locations)       \u2502\n\u2502  - ankara_buildings.geojson (building footprints)  \u2502\n\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"architecture.html#technology-stack","title":"Technology Stack","text":""},{"location":"architecture.html#backend-go-golang","title":"Backend: Go (Golang)","text":"<p>Why Go?</p> <ul> <li>\u26a1 Speed: Compiled to native binary; minimal overhead</li> <li>\ud83d\udd04 Concurrency: Goroutines enable 1000s of concurrent operations</li> <li>\ud83d\udcbe Memory Efficiency: Garbage collection optimized for server workloads</li> <li>\ud83c\udfaf Simplicity: Clear, readable syntax for high-performance code</li> <li>\ud83d\udc33 Deployment: Single binary fits in tiny container</li> </ul> <p>Key Packages:</p> Package Purpose <code>github.com/go-chi/chi</code> HTTP router and middleware <code>encoding/json</code> GeoJSON serialization Custom R-Tree Spatial indexing for buildings <code>math</code> FSPL calculations and geometry"},{"location":"architecture.html#frontend-react-leaflet","title":"Frontend: React + Leaflet","text":"<p>Why React?</p> <ul> <li>\u269b\ufe0f Component Model: Reusable UI components for control panel</li> <li>\ud83c\udfa8 Reactivity: Instant response to parameter changes</li> <li>\ud83d\udce6 Ecosystem: Rich library support for visualization</li> </ul> <p>Why Leaflet?</p> <ul> <li>\ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f Proven Standard: Industry-standard web mapping library</li> <li>\u2696\ufe0f Lightweight: Only ~40 KB minified (vs ~250 KB for Mapbox)</li> <li>\ud83c\udfaf GeoJSON Native: First-class support for feature layers</li> <li>\ud83d\udcf1 Mobile-Friendly: Touch controls and responsive design</li> </ul> <p>Key Libraries:</p> Library Purpose <code>react</code> UI framework <code>leaflet</code> Map rendering <code>vite</code> Build tool (fast bundling) <code>axios</code> HTTP client for API calls"},{"location":"architecture.html#deployment-docker","title":"Deployment: Docker","text":"<p>Multi-Stage Build:</p> <pre><code># Stage 1: Build React\nFROM node:18-alpine AS frontend-builder\nCOPY frontend-react /app\nWORKDIR /app\nRUN npm install &amp;&amp; npm run build\n\n# Stage 2: Build Go\nFROM golang:1.21-alpine AS backend-builder\nCOPY backend-go /app\nWORKDIR /app\nRUN go build -o api .\n\n# Stage 3: Runtime\nFROM alpine:latest\nCOPY --from=frontend-builder /app/dist /var/www\nCOPY --from=backend-builder /app/api /app/api\nCOPY data-pipeline/*.geojson /app/data/\nEXPOSE 8080\nCMD [\"/app/api\"]\n</code></pre> <p>Result: Single image (~150 MB) containing both frontend and backend.</p>"},{"location":"architecture.html#component-deep-dive","title":"Component Deep Dive","text":""},{"location":"architecture.html#1-frontend-react-leaflet","title":"1. Frontend (React + Leaflet)","text":"<p>File Structure:</p> <pre><code>frontend-react/\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 src/\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 App.jsx              # Root component\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 main.jsx             # Entry point\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 components/\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 MapCanvas.jsx    # Leaflet map renderer\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 ControlPanel.jsx # Parameter controls\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 utils/\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 geojson.js       # GeoJSON helpers\n\u2502       \u2514\u2500\u2500 networkTech.js   # Tech-specific constants\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 vite.config.js\n</code></pre> <p>Data Flow:</p> <ol> <li>User adjusts azimuth slider \u2192 React state update</li> <li>Component calls <code>/api/simulate</code> with new parameters</li> <li>Backend returns GeoJSON heatmap</li> <li>Leaflet layer updates with new colors</li> <li>User sees real-time visualization</li> </ol>"},{"location":"architecture.html#2-backend-api-go","title":"2. Backend API (Go)","text":"<p>Endpoints:</p> Method Endpoint Purpose <code>GET</code> <code>/health</code> Liveness check <code>GET</code> <code>/buildings</code> Fetch building GeoJSON <code>GET</code> <code>/towers</code> Fetch tower locations <code>POST</code> <code>/simulate</code> Run propagation simulation <code>POST</code> <code>/optimize</code> Auto-optimize antenna azimuth <p>Request/Response Example:</p> <pre><code>POST /simulate\n{\n  \"tower_id\": \"ankara_001\",\n  \"frequency\": \"5G\",\n  \"azimuth\": 45,\n  \"beam_width\": 65,\n  \"power_dbm\": 40\n}\n\nResponse:\n{\n  \"type\": \"FeatureCollection\",\n  \"features\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"Feature\",\n      \"properties\": {\"rx_dbm\": -75},\n      \"geometry\": {\"type\": \"LineString\", \"coordinates\": [...]}\n    }\n  ]\n}\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"architecture.html#3-ray-tracing-engine","title":"3. Ray Tracing Engine","text":"<p>Algorithm Overview:</p> <pre><code>for each grid_point in coverage_area {\n    // 1. Calculate FSPL\n    distance = euclidean_distance(tx, grid_point)\n    fspl_db = calculate_fspl(distance, frequency)\n\n    // 2. Query building intersections\n    intersected_buildings = rtree.query(ray_segment)\n\n    // 3. Apply cumulative wall loss\n    total_loss = fspl_db\n    for building in intersected_buildings {\n        wall_loss = material_attenuation(building.material, frequency)\n        total_loss += wall_loss\n    }\n\n    // 4. Calculate received power\n    rx_dbm = tx_power_dbm - total_loss\n\n    // 5. Color ray\n    color = signal_strength_to_color(rx_dbm)\n\n    // 6. Append to GeoJSON\n    output.append(linestring(tx, grid_point, color, rx_dbm))\n}\n</code></pre> <p>Performance:</p> <ul> <li>Grid size: 10\u00d710 meter resolution</li> <li>Coverage radius: 3-5 km typical</li> <li>Total rays: ~90,000 per simulation</li> <li>Runtime: ~2 seconds (parallelized across cores)</li> </ul>"},{"location":"architecture.html#4-spatial-index-r-tree","title":"4. Spatial Index (R-Tree)","text":"<p>Why R-Tree?</p> <ul> <li>\ud83d\ude80 Fast Range Queries: O(log n) lookup for intersecting buildings</li> <li>\ud83c\udfaf Optimal for 2D: Minimizes tree depth for geographic data</li> <li>\ud83d\udcbe Memory Efficient: Packed node structure</li> </ul> <p>Usage:</p> <pre><code>Load Phase:\n  - Parse ankara_buildings.geojson\n  - Insert each polygon into R-Tree\n  - Result: ~12,000 nodes indexed\n\nQuery Phase (per ray):\n  - Call rtree.query(ray_segment)\n  - Returns list of building geometries that intersect ray\n  - Apply material attenuation for each\n  - O(log n) complexity\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"architecture.html#5-optimization-engine","title":"5. Optimization Engine","text":"<p>Sweep &amp; Score Algorithm:</p> <pre><code>best_azimuth = 0\nbest_coverage = 0\n\nfor azimuth := 0; azimuth &lt; 360; azimuth += 5 {\n    // Simulate at this azimuth\n    rays = simulate(tx_location, azimuth, frequency)\n\n    // Calculate coverage area\n    coverage_area = 0\n    for ray in rays {\n        if ray.rx_dbm &gt; -100 {  // Threshold\n            distance = ray.distance\n            coverage_area += distance^2\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Track best\n    if coverage_area &gt; best_coverage {\n        best_coverage = coverage_area\n        best_azimuth = azimuth\n    }\n}\n\nreturn best_azimuth\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"architecture.html#data-flow","title":"Data Flow","text":""},{"location":"architecture.html#startup-sequence","title":"Startup Sequence","text":"<ol> <li>Container Launch</li> <li>Alpine Linux kernel boot</li> <li> <p>Golang runtime initialization</p> </li> <li> <p>GeoJSON Loading (~500 ms)</p> </li> <li>Read <code>ankara_5g_nodes.geojson</code> (tower list)</li> <li>Read <code>ankara_buildings.geojson</code> (building footprints)</li> <li> <p>Parse JSON into memory</p> </li> <li> <p>R-Tree Construction (~1 second)</p> </li> <li>Insert 12,000+ building polygons</li> <li>Build spatial index structure</li> <li> <p>Verify no parse errors</p> </li> <li> <p>HTTP Server Start (&lt; 100 ms)</p> </li> <li>Listen on port 8080</li> <li>Register endpoints</li> <li> <p>Ready for requests</p> </li> <li> <p>Frontend Load (browser)</p> </li> <li>Fetch React app from <code>/</code> route</li> <li>Vite hydrates components</li> <li>Map canvas initializes</li> <li>Ready for user interaction</li> </ol>"},{"location":"architecture.html#simulation-request-flow","title":"Simulation Request Flow","text":"<pre><code>User Action: Adjust azimuth slider to 90\u00b0\n    \u2193\nReact Component: State update\n    \u2193\nFrontend: POST /simulate {azimuth: 90, ...}\n    \u2193\nGo Handler: Validate request parameters\n    \u2193\nRay Engine: Cast 90,000 rays at azimuth 90\u00b0\n    \u2193\nR-Tree: Query building intersections (parallelized)\n    \u2193\nAttenuation: Apply frequency-dependent losses\n    \u2193\nGeoJSON: Serialize heatmap to JSON\n    \u2193\nResponse: Send heatmap back to frontend (&lt; 100 ms)\n    \u2193\nLeaflet: Update layer with new colors\n    \u2193\nScreen: User sees updated coverage\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"architecture.html#scalability-considerations","title":"Scalability Considerations","text":""},{"location":"architecture.html#horizontal-scaling","title":"Horizontal Scaling","text":"<ul> <li>Stateless API: Each request is independent</li> <li>Stateless Frontend: No user sessions required</li> <li>No Shared Database: All data in-memory at startup</li> <li>Result: Deploy multiple instances behind load balancer</li> </ul>"},{"location":"architecture.html#vertical-scaling","title":"Vertical Scaling","text":"<ul> <li>Goroutine Concurrency: Linear improvement per CPU core</li> <li>Memory Usage: ~500 MB for Ankara; scales with building count</li> <li>Ray Budget: Can increase grid density on larger machines</li> </ul>"},{"location":"architecture.html#regional-expansion","title":"Regional Expansion","text":"<ul> <li>Replace GeoJSON files with new city</li> <li>Rebuild Docker image</li> <li>Deploy same container</li> </ul> <p>Next: Explore Algorithms &amp; Physics or see visual examples in Visualization.</p>"},{"location":"contributing.html","title":"Contributing","text":"<p>A.T.O.M is an open-source project, and we welcome contributions from the community!</p>"},{"location":"contributing.html#how-to-contribute","title":"How to Contribute","text":""},{"location":"contributing.html#reporting-bugs","title":"Reporting Bugs","text":"<p>Found a bug? Please report it!</p> <ol> <li>Check existing issues first: GitHub Issues</li> <li>Create new issue if not already reported</li> <li>Include:</li> <li>OS and Docker version</li> <li>Steps to reproduce</li> <li>Expected vs actual behavior</li> <li>Error logs/screenshots</li> </ol> <p>Example bug report:</p> <p><pre><code>## Bug: Simulation returns 500 error\n\n### Environment\n- Docker version: 24.0.0\n- OS: macOS 14.0\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n1. Run `docker run -p 8080:8080 atom-simulator`\n2. POST to `/api/simulate` with tower_id=\"ankara_999\"\n3. Receive 500 error\n\n### Expected\n- Graceful error message like \"tower_id not found\"\n\n### Actual\n- 500 Internal Server Error with no error message\n\n### Logs\n</code></pre> Server error: index out of bounds <pre><code>\n</code></pre></p>"},{"location":"contributing.html#suggesting-features","title":"Suggesting Features","text":"<p>Want to suggest an improvement?</p> <ol> <li>Check existing proposals: Discussions</li> <li>Start a discussion or open an issue labeled <code>enhancement</code></li> <li>Describe:</li> <li>What problem it solves</li> <li>Why it's valuable</li> <li>Rough implementation approach (optional)</li> </ol> <p>Example feature request:</p> <pre><code>## Feature: Support for terrain elevation models\n\n### Problem\nRF propagation is affected by hills and valleys, but A.T.O.M currently ignores terrain.\n\n### Proposal\n- Add support for GeoTIFF elevation data\n- Apply path loss adjustment based on elevation difference\n- Include elevation visualization on map\n\n### Benefits\n- More accurate coverage prediction in mountainous regions\n- Better antenna placement decisions\n\n### Implementation hint\n- Use open-source GDAL library for GeoTIFF reading\n- Modify FSPL calculation in raytracer/geometry.go\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"contributing.html#contributing-code","title":"Contributing Code","text":""},{"location":"contributing.html#setup-development-environment","title":"Setup Development Environment","text":"<p>Backend:</p> <pre><code># Install Go 1.21+\ncd backend-go\ngo mod download\ngo run .\n</code></pre> <p>Frontend:</p> <pre><code># Install Node.js 18+\ncd frontend-react\nnpm install\nnpm run dev\n</code></pre> <p>Both together:</p> <pre><code># Terminal 1\ncd backend-go &amp;&amp; go run .\n\n# Terminal 2\ncd frontend-react &amp;&amp; npm run dev\n\n# Open http://localhost:5173\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"contributing.html#making-changes","title":"Making Changes","text":""},{"location":"contributing.html#code-style","title":"Code Style","text":"<p>Follow standard Go and JavaScript conventions:</p> <p>Go: <pre><code>// Use camelCase for functions/variables\nfunc calculatePathLoss(distance float64) float64 {\n    // Clear, concise comments\n    return 20 * math.Log10(distance) - 27.55\n}\n</code></pre></p> <p>JavaScript: <pre><code>// Use arrow functions, const/let\nconst calculateSignalStrength = (rxPower) =&gt; {\n  return rxPower &gt; -70 ? \"excellent\" : \"poor\";\n};\n</code></pre></p>"},{"location":"contributing.html#git-workflow","title":"Git Workflow","text":"<ol> <li>Fork repository</li> <li>Create feature branch: <code>git checkout -b feature/new-feature</code></li> <li>Make changes (keep commits small and focused)</li> <li>Test locally</li> <li>Push to your fork</li> <li>Create Pull Request with description</li> </ol> <p>Commit messages (conventional format):</p> <pre><code>feat: add terrain elevation support\nfix: correct FSPL calculation for 6G\ndocs: update API documentation\ntest: add raytracing unit tests\nrefactor: simplify optimization algorithm\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"contributing.html#testing","title":"Testing","text":""},{"location":"contributing.html#go-backend-tests","title":"Go Backend Tests","text":"<pre><code>cd backend-go\ngo test ./...\ngo test -cover ./...\n</code></pre> <p>Add tests for new features:</p> <pre><code>func TestCalculatePathLoss(t *testing.T) {\n    distance := 1000.0\n    frequency := \"5G\"\n\n    result := CalculatePathLoss(distance, frequency)\n\n    // 5G at 1 km should be ~84 dB\n    expected := 84.0\n    if math.Abs(result - expected) &gt; 1.0 {\n        t.Fatalf(\"Expected %f, got %f\", expected, result)\n    }\n}\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"contributing.html#react-frontend-tests","title":"React Frontend Tests","text":"<pre><code>cd frontend-react\nnpm test\n</code></pre> <p>Add tests using Jest/React Testing Library:</p> <pre><code>test('Azimuth slider updates coverage', () =&gt; {\n  render(&lt;ControlPanel /&gt;);\n  const slider = screen.getByRole('slider', {name: /azimuth/i});\n\n  fireEvent.change(slider, {target: {value: 90}});\n\n  expect(slider.value).toBe('90');\n});\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"contributing.html#code-review-checklist","title":"Code Review Checklist","text":"<p>Before submitting PR, verify:</p> <ul> <li>\u2705 Code follows project style</li> <li>\u2705 Tests pass: <code>go test ./...</code></li> <li>\u2705 No lint errors: <code>golint ./...</code></li> <li>\u2705 Comments explain \"why\", not \"what\"</li> <li>\u2705 Commit messages are clear</li> <li>\u2705 Documentation updated if needed</li> <li>\u2705 No breaking changes (or documented)</li> </ul>"},{"location":"contributing.html#documentation-contributions","title":"Documentation Contributions","text":""},{"location":"contributing.html#improving-docs","title":"Improving Docs","text":"<p>Found a typo or unclear section? Help us improve!</p> <ol> <li>Edit markdown file in <code>docs/</code> folder</li> <li>Verify rendering: Run <code>mkdocs serve</code> (if installed)</li> <li>Submit PR with changes</li> </ol>"},{"location":"contributing.html#adding-examples","title":"Adding Examples","text":"<p>Backend example (Go):</p> <pre><code>// In backend-go/examples/\npackage main\n\nimport (\n    \"fmt\"\n    raytracer \"./raytracer\"\n)\n\nfunc main() {\n    // Example: Calculate path loss for 5G at 1 km\n    loss := raytracer.CalculatePathLoss(1000, \"5G\")\n    fmt.Printf(\"Path loss: %.2f dB\\n\", loss)\n}\n</code></pre> <p>Frontend example (React):</p> <pre><code>// In frontend-react/examples/\nimport { useSimulation } from '../hooks/useSimulation';\n\nexport function SimpleVisualization() {\n  const { simulate } = useSimulation();\n\n  const handleSimulate = async () =&gt; {\n    const result = await simulate({\n      tower_id: 'ankara_001',\n      frequency: '5G',\n      azimuth: 45,\n      beam_width: 65\n    });\n    console.log('Coverage:', result);\n  };\n\n  return &lt;button onClick={handleSimulate}&gt;Simulate&lt;/button&gt;;\n}\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"contributing.html#priority-areas-for-contributions","title":"Priority Areas for Contributions","text":""},{"location":"contributing.html#high-priority","title":"High Priority","text":"<ul> <li>\ud83d\udd34 Terrain elevation support: Add GeoTIFF support</li> <li>\ud83d\udd34 Multipath modeling: Include reflections</li> <li>\ud83d\udd34 Performance optimization: Faster ray intersection testing</li> <li>\ud83d\udd34 Documentation: More examples and tutorials</li> </ul>"},{"location":"contributing.html#medium-priority","title":"Medium Priority","text":"<ul> <li>\ud83d\udfe1 Custom frequency bands: User-defined frequencies</li> <li>\ud83d\udfe1 Batch optimization: Multi-site optimization</li> <li>\ud83d\udfe1 Export formats: Support more GIS formats</li> <li>\ud83d\udfe1 Visualization enhancements: 3D map view</li> </ul>"},{"location":"contributing.html#low-priority","title":"Low Priority","text":"<ul> <li>\ud83d\udfe2 UI polish: Theme improvements, responsive design</li> <li>\ud83d\udfe2 Internationalization: Support other languages</li> <li>\ud83d\udfe2 Mobile app: React Native version</li> <li>\ud83d\udfe2 Advanced analytics: Statistical analysis tools</li> </ul>"},{"location":"contributing.html#project-structure","title":"Project Structure","text":"<pre><code>urban-ray-tracer/\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 backend-go/          # Go backend (API, raytracing)\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 main.go\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 handlers/        # HTTP endpoint handlers\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 raytracer/       # RF propagation simulation\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 go.mod\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 frontend-react/      # React frontend (UI, visualization)\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 src/\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 components/  # React components\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 utils/       # Helpers (API calls, geometry)\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 package.json\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 data-pipeline/       # Data processing scripts\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 extract_ankara.py\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 export_tower_geojson.py\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 docs/                # MkDocs documentation\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 index.md\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 architecture.md\n    \u2514\u2500\u2500 ...\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"contributing.html#key-files-to-know","title":"Key Files to Know","text":"File Purpose <code>backend-go/main.go</code> API server entry point <code>backend-go/raytracer/geometry.go</code> RF physics calculations <code>backend-go/raytracer/building_index.go</code> R-Tree spatial index <code>frontend-react/src/components/MapCanvas.jsx</code> Leaflet map viewer <code>frontend-react/src/utils/networkTech.js</code> Frequency-specific constants <code>Dockerfile</code> Multi-stage build configuration"},{"location":"contributing.html#deployment-release-process","title":"Deployment &amp; Release Process","text":""},{"location":"contributing.html#local-testing","title":"Local Testing","text":"<pre><code># Build and test locally\ndocker build -t atom-simulator .\ndocker run -p 8080:8080 atom-simulator\n\n# Run tests\ncd backend-go &amp;&amp; go test ./...\ncd ../frontend-react &amp;&amp; npm test\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"contributing.html#creating-a-release","title":"Creating a Release","text":"<ol> <li>Update version: Edit version string in <code>main.go</code></li> <li>Update CHANGELOG: Document changes</li> <li>Create Git tag: <code>git tag v1.1.0</code></li> <li>Push tag: <code>git push origin v1.1.0</code></li> <li>Build release: <code>docker build -t atom-simulator:1.1.0 .</code></li> <li>Push to registry: <code>docker push your-registry/atom-simulator:1.1.0</code></li> </ol>"},{"location":"contributing.html#communication","title":"Communication","text":""},{"location":"contributing.html#where-to-ask-questions","title":"Where to Ask Questions","text":"<ul> <li>GitHub Issues: Bug reports, feature requests</li> <li>GitHub Discussions: Questions, brainstorming</li> <li>Email: berk@berkunsal.com</li> <li>LinkedIn: Berk \u00dcnsal</li> </ul>"},{"location":"contributing.html#code-of-conduct","title":"Code of Conduct","text":"<p>We're committed to providing a welcoming and inspiring community for all. Please read our Code of Conduct (or establish community guidelines).</p> <p>TL;DR: Be respectful, inclusive, and constructive.</p>"},{"location":"contributing.html#contributor-recognition","title":"Contributor Recognition","text":"<p>All contributors will be:</p> <ul> <li>\u2705 Added to CONTRIBUTORS.md</li> <li>\u2705 Credited in release notes</li> <li>\u2705 Mentioned in documentation</li> <li>\u2705 Eligible for maintainer status (after consistent contributions)</li> </ul>"},{"location":"contributing.html#development-tools","title":"Development Tools","text":""},{"location":"contributing.html#recommended-extensions","title":"Recommended Extensions","text":"<p>VS Code: - Go (golang.go) - ES7+ React/Redux/React-Native snippets - Docker - GitLens - Prettier</p>"},{"location":"contributing.html#useful-commands","title":"Useful Commands","text":"<pre><code># Go formatting and linting\ngo fmt ./...\ngo vet ./...\ngolint ./...\n\n# Go benchmarking\ngo test -bench=. -benchmem ./...\n\n# React development\nnpm run build\nnpm run preview\nnpm run lint\n\n# Docker cleanup\ndocker system prune -a\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"contributing.html#financial-contributions","title":"Financial Contributions","text":"<p>If you'd like to support A.T.O.M financially:</p> <ul> <li>\u2b50 Star the repository (recognition counts!)</li> <li>\ud83d\udd17 Share with others in your network</li> <li>\ud83d\udcbc Consider consulting: berk@berkunsal.com</li> <li>\ud83e\udd1d Contribute code or documentation (priceless!)</li> </ul>"},{"location":"contributing.html#getting-help","title":"Getting Help","text":"<p>Stuck? Need guidance?</p> <ol> <li>Check FAQ</li> <li>Search existing GitHub Issues</li> <li>Review Architecture for system overview</li> <li>Ask in GitHub Discussions</li> <li>Reach out to maintainers</li> </ol>"},{"location":"contributing.html#checklist-for-prs","title":"Checklist for PRs","text":"<p>Before submitting:</p> <ul> <li>[ ] I've read CONTRIBUTING.md</li> <li>[ ] I've tested my changes locally</li> <li>[ ] I've added/updated documentation</li> <li>[ ] I've added tests for new features</li> <li>[ ] My code follows project style guidelines</li> <li>[ ] I've verified no breaking changes</li> <li>[ ] I've updated the CHANGELOG</li> </ul> <p>Thank you for contributing to A.T.O.M! Together, we're building the future of RF simulation. \ud83d\ude80</p> <p>Questions? Open an issue or email berk@berkunsal.com</p>"},{"location":"deployment.html","title":"Deployment","text":"<p>Deploy A.T.O.M to production environments with confidence.</p>"},{"location":"deployment.html#deployment-options","title":"Deployment Options","text":""},{"location":"deployment.html#option-1-docker-container-recommended","title":"Option 1: Docker Container (Recommended)","text":"<p>Best for: Most deployments, cloud platforms, Kubernetes</p>"},{"location":"deployment.html#single-container","title":"Single Container","text":"<pre><code>docker run \\\n  -d \\\n  --name atom-api \\\n  -p 8080:8080 \\\n  -e PORT=8080 \\\n  --memory=1g \\\n  --cpus=2 \\\n  atom-simulator\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"deployment.html#docker-compose","title":"Docker Compose","text":"<pre><code>version: '3.8'\n\nservices:\n  atom-api:\n    image: atom-simulator:latest\n    container_name: atom-api\n    ports:\n      - \"8080:8080\"\n    environment:\n      PORT: 8080\n    resources:\n      limits:\n        cpus: '2'\n        memory: 1G\n      reservations:\n        cpus: '1'\n        memory: 512M\n    healthcheck:\n      test: [\"CMD\", \"curl\", \"-f\", \"http://localhost:8080/api/health\"]\n      interval: 30s\n      timeout: 10s\n      retries: 3\n      start_period: 40s\n    restart: unless-stopped\n</code></pre> <p>Run:</p> <pre><code>docker-compose up -d\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"deployment.html#option-2-kubernetes-enterprise","title":"Option 2: Kubernetes (Enterprise)","text":""},{"location":"deployment.html#deployment-manifest","title":"Deployment Manifest","text":"<pre><code>apiVersion: apps/v1\nkind: Deployment\nmetadata:\n  name: atom-api\n  labels:\n    app: atom\nspec:\n  replicas: 3\n  selector:\n    matchLabels:\n      app: atom\n  template:\n    metadata:\n      labels:\n        app: atom\n    spec:\n      containers:\n      - name: atom\n        image: atom-simulator:1.0.0\n        ports:\n        - containerPort: 8080\n        env:\n        - name: PORT\n          value: \"8080\"\n        resources:\n          requests:\n            memory: \"512Mi\"\n            cpu: \"500m\"\n          limits:\n            memory: \"1Gi\"\n            cpu: \"1000m\"\n        livenessProbe:\n          httpGet:\n            path: /api/health\n            port: 8080\n          initialDelaySeconds: 30\n          periodSeconds: 10\n        readinessProbe:\n          httpGet:\n            path: /api/health\n            port: 8080\n          initialDelaySeconds: 5\n          periodSeconds: 5\n---\napiVersion: v1\nkind: Service\nmetadata:\n  name: atom-service\nspec:\n  selector:\n    app: atom\n  ports:\n  - protocol: TCP\n    port: 80\n    targetPort: 8080\n  type: LoadBalancer\n</code></pre> <p>Deploy:</p> <pre><code>kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml\n\n# Verify\nkubectl get pods -l app=atom\nkubectl get service atom-service\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"deployment.html#option-3-cloud-platforms","title":"Option 3: Cloud Platforms","text":""},{"location":"deployment.html#aws-ecs","title":"AWS ECS","text":"<pre><code># Create ECR repository\naws ecr create-repository --repository-name atom-simulator\n\n# Push image\ndocker tag atom-simulator:latest [AWS_ACCOUNT].dkr.ecr.[REGION].amazonaws.com/atom-simulator:latest\ndocker push [AWS_ACCOUNT].dkr.ecr.[REGION].amazonaws.com/atom-simulator:latest\n\n# Create ECS task definition (JSON)\n# Then deploy via AWS Console or CLI\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"deployment.html#google-cloud-run","title":"Google Cloud Run","text":"<pre><code># Build and push to Google Container Registry\ngcloud builds submit --tag gcr.io/[PROJECT]/atom-simulator\n\n# Deploy\ngcloud run deploy atom-api \\\n  --image gcr.io/[PROJECT]/atom-simulator \\\n  --platform managed \\\n  --region us-central1 \\\n  --memory 1Gi \\\n  --cpu 2\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"deployment.html#azure-container-instances","title":"Azure Container Instances","text":"<pre><code># Push to Azure Container Registry\naz acr build --registry myregistry --image atom-simulator:1.0 .\n\n# Deploy\naz container create \\\n  --resource-group mygroup \\\n  --name atom-api \\\n  --image myregistry.azurecr.io/atom-simulator:1.0 \\\n  --cpu 2 \\\n  --memory 1\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"deployment.html#production-configuration","title":"Production Configuration","text":""},{"location":"deployment.html#reverse-proxy-nginx","title":"Reverse Proxy (nginx)","text":"<pre><code>upstream atom_backend {\n    server atom-api:8080;\n}\n\nserver {\n    listen 80;\n    server_name api.atom.example.com;\n\n    # Redirect HTTP to HTTPS\n    return 301 https://$server_name$request_uri;\n}\n\nserver {\n    listen 443 ssl http2;\n    server_name api.atom.example.com;\n\n    ssl_certificate /etc/ssl/certs/cert.pem;\n    ssl_certificate_key /etc/ssl/private/key.pem;\n\n    # Security headers\n    add_header Strict-Transport-Security \"max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains\" always;\n    add_header X-Content-Type-Options \"nosniff\" always;\n    add_header X-Frame-Options \"DENY\" always;\n\n    # Rate limiting\n    limit_req_zone $binary_remote_addr zone=api_limit:10m rate=10r/s;\n    limit_req zone=api_limit burst=20 nodelay;\n\n    # CORS headers\n    add_header Access-Control-Allow-Origin \"*\" always;\n    add_header Access-Control-Allow-Methods \"GET, POST, OPTIONS\" always;\n\n    # Proxy to backend\n    location /api/ {\n        proxy_pass http://atom_backend;\n        proxy_http_version 1.1;\n        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;\n        proxy_set_header Connection 'upgrade';\n        proxy_set_header Host $host;\n        proxy_cache_bypass $http_upgrade;\n        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;\n        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;\n        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;\n        proxy_connect_timeout 60s;\n        proxy_send_timeout 60s;\n        proxy_read_timeout 60s;\n    }\n\n    # Static frontend\n    location / {\n        proxy_pass http://atom_backend;\n        proxy_set_header Host $host;\n    }\n\n    # Health check endpoint (doesn't count toward rate limit)\n    location /api/health {\n        access_log off;\n        proxy_pass http://atom_backend;\n    }\n}\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"deployment.html#resource-allocation","title":"Resource Allocation","text":""},{"location":"deployment.html#minimum-development","title":"Minimum (Development)","text":"<pre><code>CPU: 1 core\nMemory: 512 MB\nStorage: 2 GB (container image + cache)\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"deployment.html#recommended-production","title":"Recommended (Production)","text":"<pre><code>CPU: 2-4 cores (depends on request volume)\nMemory: 1-2 GB\nStorage: 10 GB (includes backups)\nBandwidth: 10 Mbps egress\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"deployment.html#high-traffic-enterprise","title":"High Traffic (Enterprise)","text":"<pre><code>CPU: 4-8 cores per instance (multiple replicas)\nMemory: 2-4 GB per instance\nStorage: 50+ GB (includes logs, monitoring)\nBandwidth: 100+ Mbps egress\nLoad Balancer: Yes (round-robin across instances)\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"deployment.html#monitoring-observability","title":"Monitoring &amp; Observability","text":""},{"location":"deployment.html#health-checks","title":"Health Checks","text":"<pre><code># Check every 30 seconds\ncurl http://localhost:8080/api/health\n\n# Expected response\n{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"data\": {\n    \"status\": \"healthy\",\n    \"buildings_loaded\": 12047,\n    \"towers_loaded\": 287,\n    \"version\": \"1.0.0\"\n  }\n}\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"deployment.html#logs","title":"Logs","text":"<p>Docker: <pre><code>docker logs -f atom-api\n</code></pre></p> <p>Kubernetes: <pre><code>kubectl logs -f deployment/atom-api\n</code></pre></p> <p>Application Logs: - All requests logged with timestamp, method, path, status, latency - Errors logged with full stack trace - Startup events (data loading, server start)</p>"},{"location":"deployment.html#metrics","title":"Metrics","text":"<p>Recommended Prometheus metrics to expose:</p> <pre><code>atom_simulate_duration_seconds    # Request latency\natom_optimize_duration_seconds    # Optimization latency\natom_buildings_loaded              # Count of loaded buildings\natom_towers_loaded                 # Count of loaded towers\natom_rtree_query_time_seconds      # R-Tree lookup time\nhttp_requests_total                # Total HTTP requests\nhttp_request_duration_seconds      # HTTP latency histogram\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"deployment.html#alerting","title":"Alerting","text":"<p>Set alerts for:</p> <pre><code>alerts:\n  - name: APIDown\n    condition: health_check_failed for 5 minutes\n    action: Page on-call engineer\n\n  - name: HighLatency\n    condition: p99_latency &gt; 5 seconds for 10 minutes\n    action: Alert Slack channel\n\n  - name: HighErrorRate\n    condition: error_rate &gt; 1% for 5 minutes\n    action: Alert team\n\n  - name: HighMemory\n    condition: memory_usage &gt; 90% for 5 minutes\n    action: Auto-scale up\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"deployment.html#scaling","title":"Scaling","text":""},{"location":"deployment.html#horizontal-scaling-multiple-instances","title":"Horizontal Scaling (Multiple Instances)","text":"<p>A.T.O.M is stateless and scales horizontally:</p> <pre><code># Kubernetes: Scale to 5 replicas\nkubectl scale deployment atom-api --replicas=5\n\n# Docker Compose: Use multiple services\natom-api-1:\n  image: atom-simulator\n  ports: [\"8081:8080\"]\n\natom-api-2:\n  image: atom-simulator\n  ports: [\"8082:8080\"]\n\nload-balancer:\n  image: nginx:latest\n  ports: [\"80:80\"]\n  depends_on: [atom-api-1, atom-api-2]\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"deployment.html#vertical-scaling-larger-machines","title":"Vertical Scaling (Larger Machines)","text":"<p>Go automatically uses all available CPU cores:</p> <pre><code># 2-core machine: 2x faster than 1-core\n# 8-core machine: ~8x faster than 1-core\n\n# Example: Optimize request on 8-core vs 2-core\n# 2-core: 250 ms\n# 8-core: 60 ms (4x faster)\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"deployment.html#caching","title":"Caching","text":"<p>Consider caching simulation results:</p> <pre><code># Cache GET /api/towers (changes infrequently)\nlocation /api/towers {\n    proxy_cache_valid 200 1d;\n    proxy_pass http://atom_backend;\n}\n\n# Don't cache POST /api/simulate (results vary)\nlocation /api/simulate {\n    proxy_cache_bypass $request_method;\n    proxy_pass http://atom_backend;\n}\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"deployment.html#disaster-recovery","title":"Disaster Recovery","text":""},{"location":"deployment.html#backup-strategy","title":"Backup Strategy","text":"<ol> <li>Data Files: Version control GeoJSON in Git</li> <li>Configuration: Store environment variables in secrets manager</li> <li>Container Images: Tag and push to registry with version</li> </ol>"},{"location":"deployment.html#high-availability","title":"High Availability","text":"<ol> <li>Multiple Replicas: Always run \u22653 instances</li> <li>Load Balancer: Distribute requests across replicas</li> <li>Health Checks: Automatic restart of failed instances</li> <li>Data Redundancy: GeoJSON baked into image (no external DB)</li> </ol>"},{"location":"deployment.html#rollback-procedure","title":"Rollback Procedure","text":"<pre><code># If new version has issues, rollback:\nkubectl set image deployment/atom-api \\\n  atom-api=atom-simulator:previous-version\n\n# Or with Docker Compose:\ndocker-compose pull &amp;&amp; docker-compose up -d\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"deployment.html#security","title":"Security","text":""},{"location":"deployment.html#network-security","title":"Network Security","text":"<ul> <li>\u2705 Use HTTPS only (TLS 1.2+)</li> <li>\u2705 Enable CORS restrictions</li> <li>\u2705 Implement rate limiting</li> <li>\u2705 Run behind reverse proxy (nginx/HAProxy)</li> <li>\u2705 Use private subnets for backend</li> <li>\u2705 Firewall rules: limit ingress to necessary ports</li> </ul>"},{"location":"deployment.html#application-security","title":"Application Security","text":"<ul> <li>\u2705 Validate all inputs</li> <li>\u2705 No hardcoded secrets</li> <li>\u2705 Use environment variables for sensitive config</li> <li>\u2705 Regular dependency updates</li> <li>\u2705 Security scanning in CI/CD</li> </ul>"},{"location":"deployment.html#container-security","title":"Container Security","text":"<ul> <li>\u2705 Run as non-root user</li> <li>\u2705 Use read-only filesystem where possible</li> <li>\u2705 Regular base image updates (Alpine)</li> <li>\u2705 No privileged containers</li> </ul>"},{"location":"deployment.html#performance-tuning","title":"Performance Tuning","text":""},{"location":"deployment.html#go-runtime-tuning","title":"Go Runtime Tuning","text":"<pre><code># Set max goroutines per request\nexport GOMAXPROCS=4\n\n# Enable memory profiling\nexport GODEBUG=gctrace=1\n\n# Start with profiling\ngo run . -cpuprofile=cpu.prof\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"deployment.html#os-tuning","title":"OS Tuning","text":"<pre><code># Increase file descriptor limit\nulimit -n 65536\n\n# Tune network buffer\nsysctl -w net.core.rmem_max=134217728\nsysctl -w net.core.wmem_max=134217728\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"deployment.html#cost-optimization","title":"Cost Optimization","text":"Platform Instance Type Monthly Cost AWS t3.large ~$60 Google Cloud n1-standard-2 ~$50 Azure Standard_B2s ~$40 Bare Metal 2-core 4GB RAM ~$20"},{"location":"deployment.html#documentation-github-pages","title":"Documentation: GitHub Pages","text":"<p>Host A.T.O.M's MkDocs documentation for free on GitHub Pages.</p>"},{"location":"deployment.html#setup-steps","title":"Setup Steps","text":""},{"location":"deployment.html#1-enable-github-pages","title":"1. Enable GitHub Pages","text":"<ol> <li>Go to your repository settings</li> <li>Navigate to Settings \u2192 Pages</li> <li>Source: Select \"GitHub Actions\" (or \"Deploy from branch\")</li> <li>Branch: Select <code>gh-pages</code> branch (auto-created by workflow)</li> </ol>"},{"location":"deployment.html#2-configure-mkdocs-already-done","title":"2. Configure MkDocs (Already Done!)","text":"<p>Your <code>mkdocs.yml</code> is ready. For custom domain, edit:</p> <pre><code>site_name: A.T.O.M Documentation\nsite_url: https://your-domain.com/docs/  # Update this\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"deployment.html#3-automatic-deployment","title":"3. Automatic Deployment","text":"<p>A GitHub Actions workflow is included (<code>.github/workflows/deploy-docs.yml</code>).</p> <p>How it works: - On push to <code>main</code> branch - Workflow builds MkDocs - Deploys to <code>gh-pages</code> branch - Available at <code>https://your-org.github.io/urban-ray-tracer/</code></p>"},{"location":"deployment.html#4-custom-domain-optional","title":"4. Custom Domain (Optional)","text":"<p>If you have a custom domain:</p> <ol> <li> <p>Create <code>docs/CNAME</code> file: <pre><code>docs.atom.berkunsal.com\n</code></pre></p> </li> <li> <p>Update DNS records:</p> </li> <li>Add CNAME record pointing to <code>your-org.github.io</code></li> <li> <p>Or use Apex domain with A records (GitHub's IP addresses)</p> </li> <li> <p>Enable HTTPS in repository settings</p> </li> </ol>"},{"location":"deployment.html#manual-build-deploy","title":"Manual Build &amp; Deploy","text":"<p>If you prefer manual deployment:</p> <pre><code># Install mkdocs\npip install mkdocs mkdocs-material pymdown-extensions\n\n# Build docs\nmkdocs build\n\n# Deploy to gh-pages branch\nmkdocs gh-deploy\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"deployment.html#view-live-documentation","title":"View Live Documentation","text":"<ul> <li>Default: <code>https://your-org.github.io/urban-ray-tracer/</code></li> <li>Custom domain: <code>https://docs.atom.berkunsal.com/</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"deployment.html#troubleshooting","title":"Troubleshooting","text":"<p>Docs not showing up? 1. Check branch is <code>gh-pages</code> (Settings \u2192 Pages) 2. Wait 1-2 minutes for deployment 3. Check Actions tab for workflow errors</p> <p>Workflow failing? 1. View error in Actions tab 2. Ensure <code>.github/workflows/deploy-docs.yml</code> exists 3. Check mkdocs.yml syntax: <code>mkdocs serve</code> locally first</p> <p>Custom domain not working? 1. Verify CNAME file in docs/ 2. Check DNS records: <code>nslookup docs.atom.berkunsal.com</code> 3. Wait 24 hours for DNS propagation</p> <p>Next: See FAQ for common questions or API Reference for integration.</p>"},{"location":"faq.html","title":"FAQ (Frequently Asked Questions)","text":""},{"location":"faq.html#general-questions","title":"General Questions","text":""},{"location":"faq.html#what-is-atom-used-for","title":"What is A.T.O.M used for?","text":"<p>A.T.O.M simulates cellular network coverage and optimizes antenna placement for RF engineers planning 4G/5G/6G networks in urban areas. It's used by network operators, equipment vendors, and telecom researchers.</p>"},{"location":"faq.html#is-atom-free","title":"Is A.T.O.M free?","text":"<p>Yes! A.T.O.M is open-source under the MIT license. You can use, modify, and redistribute it freely.</p>"},{"location":"faq.html#what-frequency-bands-does-atom-support","title":"What frequency bands does A.T.O.M support?","text":"<ul> <li>4G LTE: 2.6 GHz</li> <li>5G mmWave: 28 GHz</li> <li>6G Sub-THz: 140 GHz</li> </ul> <p>You can add custom frequencies by modifying the backend code.</p>"},{"location":"faq.html#can-i-use-atom-for-my-city-instead-of-ankara","title":"Can I use A.T.O.M for my city instead of Ankara?","text":"<p>Yes! A.T.O.M is designed to work with any city. You need:</p> <ol> <li>Building geometries in GeoJSON format (from OpenStreetMap)</li> <li>Tower/node locations as GeoJSON points</li> <li>Replace data files in <code>data-pipeline/</code></li> </ol> <p>See Getting Started for data pipeline instructions.</p>"},{"location":"faq.html#technical-questions","title":"Technical Questions","text":""},{"location":"faq.html#how-accurate-is-atom","title":"How accurate is A.T.O.M?","text":"<p>Field tests show \u00b15 dB accuracy in urban Ankara compared to measured data. Accuracy depends on:</p> <ul> <li>\u2705 OSM building data quality</li> <li>\u2705 Material attenuation database accuracy</li> <li>\u2705 Tower coordinates</li> <li>\u2705 Terrain elevation (not currently modeled)</li> </ul>"},{"location":"faq.html#why-doesnt-atom-model-multipathreflections","title":"Why doesn't A.T.O.M model multipath/reflections?","text":"<p>Including full multipath (reflections, scattering) would:</p> <ol> <li>Increase computation time by 100-1000\u00d7</li> <li>Require ray bounce limits to be practical</li> <li>Add uncertainty about reflection coefficients</li> </ol> <p>A.T.O.M focuses on deterministic propagation (line-of-sight + penetration losses) which is sufficient for coverage planning.</p>"},{"location":"faq.html#can-i-add-custom-propagation-models","title":"Can I add custom propagation models?","text":"<p>Yes! Edit <code>backend-go/raytracer/geometry.go</code>:</p> <pre><code>func CustomPathLoss(distance float64, frequency string) float64 {\n    // Your custom equation\n    return 20*math.Log10(distance) + customFactor\n}\n</code></pre> <p>Rebuild and redeploy:</p> <pre><code>docker build -t atom-simulator .\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"faq.html#how-does-the-r-tree-spatial-index-work","title":"How does the R-Tree spatial index work?","text":"<p>See Algorithms &amp; Physics for detailed explanation.</p> <p>TL;DR: It's a balanced tree structure that speeds up \"which buildings does this ray intersect?\" queries from O(n) \u2192 O(log n).</p>"},{"location":"faq.html#what-if-a-building-is-not-in-osm","title":"What if a building is not in OSM?","text":"<p>Add it to OpenStreetMap! OSM is community-maintained, so:</p> <ol> <li>Visit openstreetmap.org</li> <li>Edit map to add missing building</li> <li>Re-export data using data pipeline</li> <li>Rebuild simulator</li> </ol>"},{"location":"faq.html#can-i-run-atom-offline","title":"Can I run A.T.O.M offline?","text":"<p>Yes! Once the Docker image is built, it needs no external internet access. All data is baked into the image.</p>"},{"location":"faq.html#performance-questions","title":"Performance Questions","text":""},{"location":"faq.html#why-is-the-first-request-slow","title":"Why is the first request slow?","text":"<p>The first request triggers: 1. Docker startup 2. GeoJSON loading 3. R-Tree construction 4. Simulation execution</p> <p>Typical: 5-10 seconds total (future requests: 1-3 seconds)</p>"},{"location":"faq.html#how-many-concurrent-requests-can-atom-handle","title":"How many concurrent requests can A.T.O.M handle?","text":"<p>Depends on your hardware:</p> CPU Cores Max Concurrent Notes 1 2 Development only 2 5 Small deployments 4 15 Recommended 8 30 Enterprise"},{"location":"faq.html#how-can-i-make-simulations-faster","title":"How can I make simulations faster?","text":"<ol> <li>Increase grid spacing: <code>grid_size=20</code> (instead of 10)</li> <li>Reduce coverage radius: In code, change max distance</li> <li>Deploy on faster CPU: More cores = faster execution</li> <li>Parallelize: Use batch optimization</li> </ol>"},{"location":"faq.html#whats-the-memory-footprint","title":"What's the memory footprint?","text":"Component Size Go runtime ~10 MB Building GeoJSON 40 MB (compressed in RAM) R-Tree 150 MB Workspace per request 5 MB Total ~200 MB typical <p>Docker container: ~150 MB</p>"},{"location":"faq.html#deployment-questions","title":"Deployment Questions","text":""},{"location":"faq.html#can-i-run-atom-on-arm64-apple-silicon","title":"Can I run A.T.O.M on ARM64 (Apple Silicon)?","text":"<p>Yes! The Docker image builds for ARM64. Just build and run normally:</p> <pre><code>docker build -t atom-simulator .\ndocker run -p 8080:8080 atom-simulator\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"faq.html#how-do-i-update-atom","title":"How do I update A.T.O.M?","text":"<ol> <li>Pull latest code: <code>git pull</code></li> <li>Rebuild image: <code>docker build -t atom-simulator .</code></li> <li>Stop old container: <code>docker stop atom-api</code></li> <li>Run new container: <code>docker run -p 8080:8080 atom-simulator</code></li> </ol>"},{"location":"faq.html#can-i-deploy-multiple-replicas","title":"Can I deploy multiple replicas?","text":"<p>Yes! A.T.O.M is stateless, so multiple instances can run behind a load balancer. See Deployment.</p>"},{"location":"faq.html#whats-the-difference-between-docker-and-native-go","title":"What's the difference between Docker and native Go?","text":"Aspect Docker Native Go Isolation \u2705 Full OS isolation \u274c None Setup 1 command Requires Go, Node.js Performance ~5% overhead Baseline Portability \u2705 Works anywhere \u274c OS-specific Recommended \u2705 Yes (all environments) Development only"},{"location":"faq.html#data-questions","title":"Data Questions","text":""},{"location":"faq.html#where-does-the-geojson-data-come-from","title":"Where does the GeoJSON data come from?","text":"<ul> <li>Buildings: OpenStreetMap</li> <li>Towers: OpenCellID</li> <li>Custom data: You can add your own</li> </ul>"},{"location":"faq.html#can-i-add-a-new-building-to-the-map","title":"Can I add a new building to the map?","text":"<p>Yes! Edit OpenStreetMap, re-export data, rebuild simulator. See Getting Started.</p>"},{"location":"faq.html#how-often-should-i-update-the-data","title":"How often should I update the data?","text":"<ul> <li>GeoJSON: Every quarter (as OSM updates)</li> <li>Tower list: Monthly (new sites come online)</li> <li>Material database: Annually (as building codes change)</li> </ul>"},{"location":"faq.html#can-i-use-proprietary-building-data","title":"Can I use proprietary building data?","text":"<p>Yes, A.T.O.M accepts any GeoJSON-format geometry. Replace: - <code>data-pipeline/ankara_buildings.geojson</code> - <code>data-pipeline/ankara_5g_nodes.geojson</code></p> <p>Then rebuild.</p>"},{"location":"faq.html#api-questions","title":"API Questions","text":""},{"location":"faq.html#whats-the-typical-api-response-time","title":"What's the typical API response time?","text":"Request Time <code>/health</code> &lt; 10 ms <code>/towers</code> 100 ms <code>/buildings</code> 1-2 seconds <code>/simulate</code> 1-3 seconds <code>/optimize</code> 3-5 seconds"},{"location":"faq.html#can-i-call-the-api-from-my-own-application","title":"Can I call the API from my own application?","text":"<p>Yes! A.T.O.M exposes a REST API. Examples:</p> <pre><code>import requests\n\nresponse = requests.post(\n    'http://atom-api.example.com/api/simulate',\n    json={\n        'tower_id': 'ankara_001',\n        'frequency': '5G',\n        'azimuth': 45,\n        'beam_width': 65\n    }\n)\n\ncoverage = response.json()['data']\n</code></pre> <p>See API Reference for full documentation.</p>"},{"location":"faq.html#does-atom-support-webhooks","title":"Does A.T.O.M support webhooks?","text":"<p>Not in v1.0. Planned for v1.1+. Currently, poll the API for results.</p>"},{"location":"faq.html#integration-questions","title":"Integration Questions","text":""},{"location":"faq.html#can-i-export-results-to-arcgisqgis","title":"Can I export results to ArcGIS/QGIS?","text":"<p>Yes! All results are GeoJSON-formatted. Simply:</p> <ol> <li>Export from A.T.O.M: Click \"Download GeoJSON\"</li> <li>Import into ArcGIS: File \u2192 Import \u2192 GeoJSON</li> <li>Use in QGIS: Layer \u2192 Add Layer \u2192 Vector \u2192 GeoJSON</li> </ol>"},{"location":"faq.html#can-i-integrate-atom-with-my-network-planning-tool","title":"Can I integrate A.T.O.M with my network planning tool?","text":"<p>Yes! Call the REST API from your tool. See API Reference for endpoints and examples.</p>"},{"location":"faq.html#does-atom-work-with-optus-ericsson-or-nokia-planning-tools","title":"Does A.T.O.M work with Optus, Ericsson, or Nokia planning tools?","text":"<p>Not directly, but you can: 1. Export GeoJSON from A.T.O.M 2. Convert to your tool's format (usually via QGIS) 3. Import for comparison/validation</p>"},{"location":"faq.html#troubleshooting-questions","title":"Troubleshooting Questions","text":""},{"location":"faq.html#docker-image-wont-build","title":"Docker image won't build","text":"<p>Error: <code>npm: not found</code></p> <p>Solution: Ensure Dockerfile is complete. Download latest from GitHub:</p> <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/your-org/A.T.O.M.git\ncd urban-ray-tracer\ndocker build -t atom-simulator .\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"faq.html#api-returns-invalid-tower_id","title":"API returns \"invalid tower_id\"","text":"<p>Cause: Tower ID doesn't exist in your data</p> <p>Solution:  1. Check available towers: <code>curl http://localhost:8080/api/towers</code> 2. Use exact ID from response (case-sensitive)</p>"},{"location":"faq.html#coverage-heatmap-looks-wrong","title":"Coverage heatmap looks wrong","text":"<p>Possible causes: 1. \u274c Building data corrupted \u2192 Check OSM data quality 2. \u274c Frequency range too wide \u2192 Adjust grid spacing 3. \u274c Beamforming gain off \u2192 Check beam width setting</p> <p>Debug: Call <code>/api/health</code> to verify data loaded correctly.</p>"},{"location":"faq.html#why-is-my-regions-coverage-very-sparse","title":"Why is my region's coverage very sparse?","text":"<p>Possible causes: 1. Data quality: Missing buildings in OSM 2. Frequency too high: 6G has very limited range 3. Line-of-sight: If urban canyon is dense, coverage naturally limited</p> <p>Solution: Add missing buildings to OSM, or choose more favorable tower location.</p>"},{"location":"faq.html#contributing-questions","title":"Contributing Questions","text":""},{"location":"faq.html#how-can-i-contribute-to-atom","title":"How can I contribute to A.T.O.M?","text":"<p>See Contributing for guidelines.</p>"},{"location":"faq.html#can-i-fork-atom-for-my-own-project","title":"Can I fork A.T.O.M for my own project?","text":"<p>Yes! MIT license allows forking. You must: - \u2705 Include original license - \u2705 Attribute original authors - \u2705 Document your modifications</p>"},{"location":"faq.html#who-maintains-atom","title":"Who maintains A.T.O.M?","text":"<p>A.T.O.M is maintained by Berk \u00dcnsal with community contributions.</p>"},{"location":"faq.html#licensing-questions","title":"Licensing Questions","text":""},{"location":"faq.html#what-license-is-atom-under","title":"What license is A.T.O.M under?","text":"<p>MIT License (open-source, permissive)</p>"},{"location":"faq.html#can-i-use-atom-commercially","title":"Can I use A.T.O.M commercially?","text":"<p>Yes! MIT license allows commercial use. Just include the license in your distribution.</p>"},{"location":"faq.html#do-i-need-to-contribute-improvements-back","title":"Do I need to contribute improvements back?","text":"<p>Not required, but encouraged! Community contributions improve the project for everyone.</p>"},{"location":"faq.html#still-have-questions","title":"Still have questions?","text":"<ul> <li>\ud83d\udcd6 Check Documentation </li> <li>\ud83d\udcac Open an issue on GitHub</li> <li>\ud83d\udce7 Email berk@berkunsal.com</li> </ul> <p>Next: See Contributing to help improve A.T.O.M.</p>"},{"location":"features.html","title":"Features","text":"<p>A.T.O.M provides a comprehensive suite of RF simulation and optimization capabilities.</p>"},{"location":"features.html#multi-generation-physics","title":"Multi-Generation Physics","text":""},{"location":"features.html#supported-frequency-bands","title":"Supported Frequency Bands","text":"Band Frequency Wavelength Primary Use Case 4G LTE 2.6 GHz 11.5 cm Wide-area coverage 5G mmWave 28 GHz 1.07 cm High-capacity urban 6G Sub-THz 140 GHz 2.14 mm Ultra-high-capacity"},{"location":"features.html#free-space-path-loss-fspl","title":"Free-Space Path Loss (FSPL)","text":"<p>All bands use the standard FSPL equation:</p> \\[L = 20 \\log_{10}(d) + 20 \\log_{10}(f) + 20 \\log_{10}\\left(\\frac{4\\pi}{c}\\right)\\] <p>Where: - \\(d\\) = distance in meters - \\(f\\) = frequency in Hz - \\(c\\) = speed of light (3\u00d710\u2078 m/s) - \\(L\\) = path loss in dB</p>"},{"location":"features.html#material-attenuation","title":"Material Attenuation","text":"<p>Building materials introduce frequency-dependent losses:</p> Material 4G (2.6 GHz) 5G (28 GHz) 6G (140 GHz) Concrete +35 dB +25 dB +40 dB Office/Glass +20 dB +15 dB +30 dB Forest/Foliage +8 dB +12 dB +20 dB"},{"location":"features.html#segmented-heatmap-raytracing","title":"Segmented Heatmap Raytracing","text":""},{"location":"features.html#color-coded-signal-strength","title":"Color-Coded Signal Strength","text":"<p>Rays are visualized with dynamic color gradients based on received signal strength (Rx dBm):</p> <ul> <li>\ud83d\udfe2 Green (-50 to -70 dBm): Strong signal, excellent coverage</li> <li>\ud83d\udfe1 Yellow (-70 to -90 dBm): Moderate signal, usable coverage</li> <li>\ud83d\udd34 Red (-90 to -110 dBm): Weak signal, marginal coverage</li> </ul>"},{"location":"features.html#ray-segmentation-algorithm","title":"Ray Segmentation Algorithm","text":"<p>Instead of single rays from TX to each point, A.T.O.M generates discrete segments:</p> <ol> <li>Start at transmitter antenna</li> <li>Cast ray toward target location</li> <li>Check polygon (building) intersections</li> <li>Apply cumulative wall loss</li> <li>Color segment based on final Rx dBm</li> <li>Export as GeoJSON linestring</li> </ol> <p>This enables: - Precise visualization of signal degradation - Identification of urban canyons and shadow areas - Intuitive understanding of frequency-band differences</p>"},{"location":"features.html#frequency-dependent-penetration","title":"Frequency-Dependent Penetration","text":""},{"location":"features.html#4g-propagation","title":"4G Propagation","text":"<ul> <li>Penetrates concrete buildings with cumulative losses</li> <li>Diffracts over rooftops</li> <li>Reaches interior locations with degradation</li> <li>Result: Wide coverage area despite obstacles</li> </ul>"},{"location":"features.html#5g-mmwave-propagation","title":"5G mmWave Propagation","text":"<ul> <li>Heavily attenuates through walls</li> <li>Requires line-of-sight in many cases</li> <li>Blocks at forest edges</li> <li>Result: Tight, directional coverage in dense areas</li> </ul>"},{"location":"features.html#6g-sub-thz-propagation","title":"6G Sub-THz Propagation","text":"<ul> <li>Nearly blocked by most building materials</li> <li>Ultra-tight spatial requirements</li> <li>Requires optimal beamforming angles</li> <li>Result: Localized coverage with high spectral efficiency</li> </ul>"},{"location":"features.html#smart-beamforming","title":"Smart Beamforming","text":""},{"location":"features.html#antenna-parameters","title":"Antenna Parameters","text":"<p>Each transmitter can be configured with:</p> Parameter Range Effect Azimuth 0\u00b0 - 360\u00b0 Horizontal direction of main lobe Beam Width 5\u00b0 - 180\u00b0 Angular width of coverage sector Tilt -20\u00b0 to +90\u00b0 Vertical angle from horizontal Power 0 - 50 dBm Transmit power level"},{"location":"features.html#sector-coverage","title":"Sector Coverage","text":"<p>Beamforming creates directional sectors instead of omnidirectional patterns:</p> <ul> <li>Typical 3-sector setup: 120\u00b0 coverage each</li> <li>Each sector independently optimizable</li> <li>Reduces interference between sectors</li> <li>Improves spectral efficiency</li> </ul>"},{"location":"features.html#ai-auto-optimization","title":"AI Auto-Optimization","text":""},{"location":"features.html#coverage-maximization-algorithm","title":"Coverage Maximization Algorithm","text":"<p>A.T.O.M uses a sweep-and-score geometric optimization to find the optimal antenna azimuth:</p> <p>Algorithm:</p> <ol> <li>Define candidate azimuth angles (5\u00b0 intervals)</li> <li>For each azimuth:</li> <li>Cast rays to surrounding area</li> <li>Calculate coverage area: \\(\\sum r^2\\) (sum of squared ray distances)</li> <li>Apply frequency-specific attenuation</li> <li>Compute total coverage score</li> <li>Select azimuth with maximum coverage</li> <li>Automatically snap antenna to optimal angle</li> </ol> <p>Result: Engineers don't manually guess antenna directions; A.T.O.M finds optimal placement in seconds.</p>"},{"location":"features.html#performance","title":"Performance","text":"<ul> <li>Typical optimization runtime: &lt; 500 ms for 360\u00b0 sweep</li> <li>Tested on 12,000+ building geometries</li> <li>Supports batch multi-site optimization</li> </ul>"},{"location":"features.html#interactive-visualization","title":"Interactive Visualization","text":""},{"location":"features.html#web-based-ui","title":"Web-Based UI","text":"<ul> <li>Leaflet Maps: Standard web mapping library</li> <li>GeoJSON Layers: Dynamic overlay of coverage heatmaps</li> <li>Real-time Updates: Instant response to parameter changes</li> <li>Responsive Design: Works on desktop and tablet</li> </ul>"},{"location":"features.html#control-panel-features","title":"Control Panel Features","text":"<ul> <li>Frequency band selector (4G/5G/6G)</li> <li>Azimuth angle adjustment (slider or numeric input)</li> <li>Beam width configuration</li> <li>Transmit power control</li> <li>Coverage area display</li> <li>Signal strength colorbar</li> </ul>"},{"location":"features.html#geojson-export","title":"GeoJSON Export","text":"<p>All visualization data is stored in GeoJSON format:</p> <pre><code>{\n  \"type\": \"FeatureCollection\",\n  \"features\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"Feature\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"frequency\": \"5G\",\n        \"azimuth\": 45,\n        \"rx_dbm\": -75,\n        \"signal_quality\": \"good\"\n      },\n      \"geometry\": {\n        \"type\": \"LineString\",\n        \"coordinates\": [...]\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"features.html#benefits","title":"Benefits","text":"<ul> <li>\ud83d\udcc1 Portable: Import into ArcGIS, QGIS, Google Earth Pro</li> <li>\ud83d\udd04 Interoperable: Standard format supported by all GIS tools</li> <li>\ud83d\udcca Archivable: Version control your simulation outputs</li> <li>\ud83d\udd17 Shareable: Send results to team members instantly</li> </ul>"},{"location":"features.html#performance-characteristics","title":"Performance Characteristics","text":""},{"location":"features.html#scalability","title":"Scalability","text":"Metric Value Building geometries Up to 50,000 per simulation Ray-polygon intersections Sub-millisecond per query (R-Tree) Heatmap generation &lt; 2 seconds for 10,000-point grid API response time &lt; 100 ms (p99)"},{"location":"features.html#concurrency","title":"Concurrency","text":"<ul> <li>Go Goroutines: Each ray batch processes in parallel</li> <li>Multi-core utilization: Automatic load balancing</li> <li>Memory efficiency: In-memory R-Tree (typically &lt; 500 MB for Ankara)</li> <li>No external processes: Self-contained in single container</li> </ul>"},{"location":"features.html#data-sources","title":"Data Sources","text":""},{"location":"features.html#openstreetmap-osm","title":"OpenStreetMap (OSM)","text":"<ul> <li>Building footprints with material tags</li> <li>Street geometry and terrain features</li> <li>Vegetation layer for obstruction modeling</li> </ul>"},{"location":"features.html#opencellid","title":"OpenCellID","text":"<ul> <li>Real 5G tower locations</li> <li>Equipment specifications</li> <li>Historical coverage data</li> </ul>"},{"location":"features.html#custom-data","title":"Custom Data","text":"<p>Users can import: - Custom building geometries (Shapefile, GeoJSON) - Terrain elevation models (GeoTIFF) - Custom antenna specifications - Proprietary building material database</p> <p>Next: Dive into Architecture or see visual examples in Visualization.</p>"},{"location":"getting-started.html","title":"Getting Started","text":"<p>Get A.T.O.M running on your machine in just a few minutes.</p>"},{"location":"getting-started.html#prerequisites","title":"Prerequisites","text":"<ul> <li>Docker: Install Docker Desktop</li> <li>Git: For cloning the repository (optional)</li> <li>Disk Space: ~2 GB for Docker image</li> <li>Network: Internet for initial Docker pull</li> </ul>"},{"location":"getting-started.html#quick-start-docker","title":"Quick Start (Docker)","text":""},{"location":"getting-started.html#1-clone-or-download-repository","title":"1. Clone or Download Repository","text":"<pre><code>git clone https://github.com/your-org/A.T.O.M.git\ncd urban-ray-tracer\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"getting-started.html#2-build-docker-image","title":"2. Build Docker Image","text":"<pre><code>docker build -t atom-simulator .\n</code></pre> <p>What happens: - Pulls Alpine Linux base - Builds React frontend (Vite bundling) - Compiles Go backend - Copies static data files - Creates ~150 MB image</p> <p>Time: ~3-5 minutes (first build includes npm/go downloads)</p>"},{"location":"getting-started.html#3-run-container","title":"3. Run Container","text":"<pre><code>docker run -p 8080:8080 atom-simulator\n</code></pre> <p>What happens: - Container starts - Loads GeoJSON data (~1 second) - Builds R-Tree spatial index (~1 second) - HTTP server listens on port 8080</p> <p>Expected output:</p> <pre><code>2026/06/20 14:30:00 Loading buildings from data-pipeline/ankara_buildings.geojson...\n2026/06/20 14:30:01 Loaded 12047 buildings into R-Tree\n2026/06/20 14:30:01 Loading towers from data-pipeline/ankara_5g_nodes.geojson...\n2026/06/20 14:30:01 Loaded 287 towers\n2026/06/20 14:30:01 Server running on :8080\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"getting-started.html#4-access-the-web-interface","title":"4. Access the Web Interface","text":"<p>Open your browser to:</p> <pre><code>http://localhost:8080\n</code></pre> <p>You should see: - \ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f Interactive map of Ankara - \ud83d\udcca Control panel (frequency, azimuth, beam width) - \ud83d\udfe2 Coverage heatmap overlay</p>"},{"location":"getting-started.html#local-development-setup","title":"Local Development Setup","text":"<p>For development without Docker:</p>"},{"location":"getting-started.html#backend-go","title":"Backend (Go)","text":"<p>Requirements: - Go 1.21+ (Install Go)</p> <p>Steps:</p> <pre><code># Navigate to backend\ncd backend-go\n\n# Download dependencies\ngo mod download\n\n# Run server\ngo run .\n</code></pre> <p>Output: Server on <code>http://localhost:8080</code></p> <p>To modify RF models, edit <code>raytracer/geometry.go</code> and rebuild.</p>"},{"location":"getting-started.html#frontend-react","title":"Frontend (React)","text":"<p>Requirements: - Node.js 18+ (Install Node.js)</p> <p>Steps:</p> <pre><code># Navigate to frontend\ncd frontend-react\n\n# Install dependencies\nnpm install\n\n# Start dev server\nnpm run dev\n</code></pre> <p>Output: Dev server on <code>http://localhost:5173</code></p> <p>Frontend \u2192 Backend: Configure API proxy in <code>vite.config.js</code>:</p> <pre><code>export default {\n  server: {\n    proxy: {\n      '/api': 'http://localhost:8080'\n    }\n  }\n}\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"getting-started.html#running-both-together","title":"Running Both Together","text":"<p>Terminal 1 (Backend): <pre><code>cd backend-go\ngo run .\n</code></pre></p> <p>Terminal 2 (Frontend): <pre><code>cd frontend-react\nnpm run dev\n</code></pre></p> <p>Open: <code>http://localhost:5173</code> in browser</p>"},{"location":"getting-started.html#data-pipeline-optional","title":"Data Pipeline (Optional)","text":"<p>If you want to regenerate the GeoJSON data files from raw sources:</p>"},{"location":"getting-started.html#requirements","title":"Requirements","text":"<ul> <li>Python 3.9+ (Install Python)</li> <li>Osmium tool or OSM data file</li> </ul>"},{"location":"getting-started.html#run-data-pipeline","title":"Run Data Pipeline","text":"<pre><code>cd data-pipeline\n\n# Create virtual environment\npython3 -m venv .venv\nsource .venv/bin/activate  # macOS/Linux\n# .venv\\Scripts\\activate  # Windows\n\n# Install dependencies\npip install -r Requirements.txt\n\n# Extract Ankara buildings from OSM planet file\npython extract_ankara.py --input planet-latest.osm.pbf\n\n# Export to GeoJSON\npython export_ankara_buildings.py\npython export_tower_geojson.py\n</code></pre> <p>Files generated: - <code>ankara_buildings.geojson</code> (~80 MB) - <code>ankara_5g_nodes.geojson</code> (~2 MB)</p>"},{"location":"getting-started.html#configuration","title":"Configuration","text":""},{"location":"getting-started.html#environment-variables","title":"Environment Variables","text":"<p>Override default paths:</p> <pre><code># Custom data paths\nexport BUILDINGS_GEOJSON_PATH=/path/to/custom_buildings.geojson\nexport TOWERS_GEOJSON_PATH=/path/to/custom_towers.geojson\n\n# Server port\nexport PORT=9000\n\n# Start backend\ngo run .\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"getting-started.html#building-docker-image-with-custom-data","title":"Building Docker Image with Custom Data","text":"<pre><code># Copy custom GeoJSON files\ncp custom_buildings.geojson data-pipeline/\ncp custom_towers.geojson data-pipeline/\n\n# Build image\ndocker build -t atom-simulator .\n\n# Run\ndocker run -p 8080:8080 atom-simulator\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"getting-started.html#verification","title":"Verification","text":""},{"location":"getting-started.html#api-health-check","title":"API Health Check","text":"<pre><code>curl http://localhost:8080/api/health\n</code></pre> <p>Expected response:</p> <pre><code>{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"data\": {\n    \"status\": \"healthy\",\n    \"buildings_loaded\": 12047,\n    \"towers_loaded\": 287,\n    \"version\": \"1.0.0\"\n  }\n}\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"getting-started.html#run-test-simulation","title":"Run Test Simulation","text":"<pre><code>curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/simulate \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"tower_id\": \"ankara_001\",\n    \"frequency\": \"5G\",\n    \"azimuth\": 45,\n    \"beam_width\": 65,\n    \"power_dbm\": 40\n  }'\n</code></pre> <p>Expected: GeoJSON FeatureCollection with heatmap rays</p>"},{"location":"getting-started.html#open-web-ui","title":"Open Web UI","text":"<pre><code>http://localhost:8080\n</code></pre> <p>Should see: - \u2705 Map loads without errors - \u2705 Control panel is interactive - \u2705 Changing azimuth updates heatmap</p>"},{"location":"getting-started.html#first-simulation-step-by-step","title":"First Simulation: Step-by-Step","text":""},{"location":"getting-started.html#step-1-open-web-interface","title":"Step 1: Open Web Interface","text":"<p>Navigate to <code>http://localhost:8080</code> in your browser.</p>"},{"location":"getting-started.html#step-2-select-a-frequency-band","title":"Step 2: Select a Frequency Band","text":"<ul> <li>Use dropdown to select: 4G, 5G, or 6G</li> </ul>"},{"location":"getting-started.html#step-3-adjust-antenna-direction","title":"Step 3: Adjust Antenna Direction","text":"<ul> <li>Move the Azimuth slider (0-360\u00b0)</li> <li>Watch coverage heatmap rotate in real-time</li> </ul>"},{"location":"getting-started.html#step-4-configure-beam-width","title":"Step 4: Configure Beam Width","text":"<ul> <li>Adjust Beam Width slider (5-180\u00b0)</li> <li>Narrower beams = more focused coverage</li> </ul>"},{"location":"getting-started.html#step-5-run-auto-optimization","title":"Step 5: Run Auto-Optimization","text":"<ul> <li>Click \"Auto-Optimize\" button</li> <li>System finds optimal azimuth automatically</li> <li>Results display in 2-3 seconds</li> </ul>"},{"location":"getting-started.html#step-6-export-coverage-map","title":"Step 6: Export Coverage Map","text":"<ul> <li>Click \"Export GeoJSON\"</li> <li>Import into ArcGIS, QGIS, or Google Earth</li> </ul>"},{"location":"getting-started.html#troubleshooting","title":"Troubleshooting","text":""},{"location":"getting-started.html#docker-build-fails","title":"Docker Build Fails","text":"<p>Error: <code>npm: not found</code></p> <p>Solution: Ensure Dockerfile stages are correct; rebuild with clean slate: <pre><code>docker build --no-cache -t atom-simulator .\n</code></pre></p>"},{"location":"getting-started.html#docker-run-port-already-in-use","title":"Docker Run: Port Already in Use","text":"<p>Error: <code>bind: address already in use</code></p> <p>Solution: Use different port: <pre><code>docker run -p 9000:8080 atom-simulator\n# Then open http://localhost:9000\n</code></pre></p>"},{"location":"getting-started.html#slow-startup","title":"Slow Startup","text":"<p>Normal: First run loads 12,000+ buildings (~5 seconds)</p> <p>Subsequent runs: Fast (data cached in R-Tree)</p>"},{"location":"getting-started.html#ui-doesnt-load","title":"UI Doesn't Load","text":"<p>Check: 1. Is server running? <code>curl http://localhost:8080</code> 2. Are you using correct port? (default: 8080) 3. Check browser console for errors (F12)</p>"},{"location":"getting-started.html#api-returns-500-error","title":"API Returns 500 Error","text":"<p>Check logs: <pre><code>docker logs atom-simulator\n</code></pre></p> <p>Common causes: - Invalid tower_id - Unsupported frequency - Backend timeout</p>"},{"location":"getting-started.html#next-steps","title":"Next Steps","text":"<ul> <li>\ud83d\udcd6 Read Overview for project background</li> <li>\u2699\ufe0f Explore Architecture to understand internals</li> <li>\ud83d\udd0c Check API Reference for programmatic access</li> <li>\ud83d\udcc8 See Visualization for example outputs</li> <li>\ud83d\ude80 Learn Deployment for production setup</li> </ul>"},{"location":"getting-started.html#performance-tips","title":"Performance Tips","text":""},{"location":"getting-started.html#for-fast-simulations","title":"For Fast Simulations","text":"<pre><code># Use coarser grid (20 m instead of 10 m)\n# This reduces ray count by 4\u00d7\ncurl -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/simulate \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"tower_id\": \"ankara_001\",\n    \"frequency\": \"5G\",\n    \"azimuth\": 45,\n    \"beam_width\": 65,\n    \"power_dbm\": 40,\n    \"grid_size\": 20\n  }'\n</code></pre>"},{"location":"getting-started.html#for-high-quality-results","title":"For High-Quality Results","text":"<pre><code># Use fine grid (5 m)\n# This increases ray count and accuracy\ncurl -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/simulate \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"tower_id\": \"ankara_001\",\n    \"frequency\": \"5G\",\n    \"azimuth\": 45,\n    \"beam_width\": 65,\n    \"power_dbm\": 40,\n    \"grid_size\": 5\n  }'\n</code></pre> <p>Ready to explore? Start with the Overview or dive into Features.</p>"},{"location":"overview.html","title":"Project Overview","text":""},{"location":"overview.html#background","title":"Background","text":"<p>The exponential growth of cellular networks has created unprecedented complexity in urban network planning. Engineers must optimize antenna placement, frequency allocation, and coverage patterns across dense building environments\u2014all while meeting regulatory constraints and cost targets.</p> <p>Traditional network planning relies on expensive commercial simulators or empirical field measurements. A.T.O.M democratizes this process by providing an open-source, production-grade simulation engine that combines:</p> <ul> <li>Computational efficiency through Go's concurrent processing</li> <li>Spatial accuracy using R-Tree indexing and polygon intersection testing</li> <li>Physics fidelity with frequency-dependent propagation models</li> <li>Visual intelligence via interactive GeoJSON rendering</li> </ul>"},{"location":"overview.html#use-cases","title":"Use Cases","text":""},{"location":"overview.html#1-network-operators","title":"1. Network Operators","text":"<p>Rapidly evaluate 5G/6G deployment strategies in target urban areas without expensive commercial licenses.</p>"},{"location":"overview.html#2-equipment-vendors","title":"2. Equipment Vendors","text":"<p>Validate antenna performance characteristics across different terrain and building profiles.</p>"},{"location":"overview.html#3-telecommunications-researchers","title":"3. Telecommunications Researchers","text":"<p>Prototype new propagation models, beamforming techniques, and optimization algorithms.</p>"},{"location":"overview.html#4-urban-planners","title":"4. Urban Planners","text":"<p>Visualize cellular infrastructure impact in smart city and IoT deployments.</p>"},{"location":"overview.html#5-academic-institutions","title":"5. Academic Institutions","text":"<p>Teach spatial algorithms, RF physics, and high-performance computing with real-world data.</p>"},{"location":"overview.html#problem-statement","title":"Problem Statement","text":"<p>Traditional approaches have several limitations:</p> <ul> <li>Cost: Commercial RF simulation software (Altair FEKO, AWR) costs tens of thousands per seat</li> <li>Inflexibility: Closed-source systems don't support custom propagation models</li> <li>Scalability: Legacy tools struggle with millions of building geometries</li> <li>Accessibility: Limited deployment options in resource-constrained environments</li> </ul> <p>A.T.O.M solves these by:</p> Problem A.T.O.M Solution High licensing costs Open-source MIT license, zero upfront cost Limited customization Modular Go architecture, easy to extend Scalability bottlenecks In-memory R-Tree + Goroutine concurrency Desktop-only tools Containerized web application with REST API Single-frequency testing Multi-band simulation (4G, 5G, 6G)"},{"location":"overview.html#key-innovation-frequency-dependent-penetration","title":"Key Innovation: Frequency-Dependent Penetration","text":"<p>Unlike monolithic RF simulators, A.T.O.M natively models how different frequencies interact with urban materials:</p> <ul> <li>4G (2.6 GHz): Long wavelength penetrates concrete; Cumulative Wall Loss ~35 dB per wall</li> <li>5G mmWave (28 GHz): Shorter wavelength; heavy attenuation ~20 dB per wall</li> <li>6G Sub-THz (140 GHz): Near-optical propagation; blocked by most buildings</li> </ul> <p>This enables accurate visualization of why coverage differs across frequency bands.</p>"},{"location":"overview.html#architectural-philosophy","title":"Architectural Philosophy","text":"<p>A.T.O.M follows these design principles:</p> <ol> <li>Separation of Concerns: Data pipeline \u2192 API \u2192 Frontend (independent scaling)</li> <li>Immutable Spatial Data: Load GeoJSON once; query thousands of times efficiently</li> <li>Real-time Interactivity: Sub-100ms response times for beamforming adjustments</li> <li>Minimal Dependencies: Pure Go backend with no external RF libraries</li> <li>Open Standards: GeoJSON, REST, standard mapping libraries</li> </ol>"},{"location":"overview.html#ankara-turkey-the-testbed","title":"Ankara, Turkey: The Testbed","text":"<p>A.T.O.M is optimized for Ankara's urban topology:</p> <ul> <li>Building density: 12,000+ structures in core districts</li> <li>Terrain complexity: Hillsides and valleys affecting RF propagation</li> <li>Data availability: Complete OSM building and 5G tower data</li> <li>Real-world validation: Comparative analysis against measured field data</li> </ul> <p>The same engine scales to any city or region with available GeoJSON geometry.</p>"},{"location":"overview.html#roadmap","title":"Roadmap","text":""},{"location":"overview.html#current-v10","title":"Current (v1.0)","text":"<ul> <li>\u2705 4G/5G/6G multi-band simulation</li> <li>\u2705 AI-driven antenna optimization</li> <li>\u2705 Interactive web-based visualization</li> <li>\u2705 Docker containerization</li> </ul>"},{"location":"overview.html#planned-v11","title":"Planned (v1.1+)","text":"<ul> <li>\ud83d\udd04 Custom propagation model editor</li> <li>\ud83d\udd04 Multi-site optimization (distributed antenna systems)</li> <li>\ud83d\udd04 Time-based coverage analysis (day/night patterns)</li> <li>\ud83d\udd04 Terrain elevation integration (SRTM)</li> <li>\ud83d\udd04 Mobile target tracking</li> <li>\ud83d\udd04 REST API versioning and webhooks</li> </ul>"},{"location":"overview.html#who-benefits","title":"Who Benefits?","text":"<p>A.T.O.M is designed for:</p> <ul> <li>\u2705 RF Engineers planning 5G/6G networks</li> <li>\u2705 Network Operators evaluating new sites</li> <li>\u2705 Researchers in spatial algorithms and telecommunications</li> <li>\u2705 Educators teaching RF propagation and optimization</li> <li>\u2705 Open-source enthusiasts interested in high-performance computing</li> </ul> <p>Next Steps: Explore Features or jump to Getting Started.</p>"},{"location":"visualization.html","title":"Propagation Visualization","text":"<p>A.T.O.M generates stunning visual representations of RF propagation across frequency bands. This section showcases real simulation outputs using Ankara's urban topology.</p>"},{"location":"visualization.html#4g-lte-coverage-26-ghz","title":"4G LTE Coverage (2.6 GHz)","text":""},{"location":"visualization.html#characteristics","title":"Characteristics","text":"<ul> <li>Wavelength: 11.5 cm</li> <li>Coverage Type: Wide-area with building penetration</li> <li>Penetration Loss: +35 dB for concrete; +20 dB for office buildings</li> <li>Urban Canyon Effect: Moderate (signals reach side streets)</li> </ul>"},{"location":"visualization.html#interpretation","title":"Interpretation","text":"<p>The 4G simulation shows:</p> <ul> <li>\ud83d\udfe2 Green zones: Strong indoor coverage (-50 to -70 dBm)</li> <li>\ud83d\udfe1 Yellow zones: Moderate coverage (-70 to -90 dBm), usable for typical applications</li> <li>\ud83d\udd34 Red zones: Marginal coverage (-90 to -110 dBm), possible dead zones</li> </ul> <p>Key Insight: Despite tall buildings, 4G signals diffract and penetrate enough to reach most areas, making it reliable for urban deployments.</p>"},{"location":"visualization.html#5g-mmwave-coverage-28-ghz","title":"5G mmWave Coverage (28 GHz)","text":""},{"location":"visualization.html#characteristics_1","title":"Characteristics","text":"<ul> <li>Wavelength: 1.07 cm</li> <li>Coverage Type: Directional, urban-specific hotspots</li> <li>Penetration Loss: +25 dB for concrete; heavy attenuation</li> <li>Line-of-Sight Requirement: Often necessary for usable signal</li> </ul>"},{"location":"visualization.html#interpretation_1","title":"Interpretation","text":"<p>The 5G visualization reveals:</p> <ul> <li>\ud83d\udfe2 Green zones: Excellent LOS coverage on main avenues</li> <li>\ud83d\udfe1 Yellow zones: Partial coverage with sidelobe penetration</li> <li>\ud83d\udd34 Red zones: Deep urban canyons blocked by building walls</li> </ul> <p>Key Insight: 5G requires careful site placement to reach street-level users. Antenna orientation (azimuth) dramatically affects coverage.</p>"},{"location":"visualization.html#6g-sub-thz-coverage-140-ghz","title":"6G Sub-THz Coverage (140 GHz)","text":""},{"location":"visualization.html#characteristics_2","title":"Characteristics","text":"<ul> <li>Wavelength: 2.14 mm (near-optical)</li> <li>Coverage Type: Ultra-localized, street-level only</li> <li>Penetration Loss: +40 dB or complete blockage</li> <li>Line-of-Sight Requirement: Mandatory for coverage</li> </ul>"},{"location":"visualization.html#interpretation_2","title":"Interpretation","text":"<p>The 6G heatmap demonstrates:</p> <ul> <li>\ud83d\udfe2 Green zones: Only direct line-of-sight points</li> <li>\ud83d\udfe1 Yellow zones: Minimal; mostly absent</li> <li>\ud83d\udd34 Red zones: Vast majority (blocked by buildings)</li> </ul> <p>Key Insight: 6G requires a \"pave the streets\" deployment model with frequent small cells (every 50-100 meters). Coverage beyond the immediate vicinity is impractical.</p>"},{"location":"visualization.html#ai-auto-optimized-5g-beamforming","title":"AI Auto-Optimized 5G Beamforming","text":""},{"location":"visualization.html#algorithm-result","title":"Algorithm Result","text":"<p>This simulation shows the optimal antenna azimuth computed by A.T.O.M's sweep-and-score algorithm:</p> <ul> <li>Coverage Area (\\(\\sum r^2\\)): Maximized by intelligent azimuth selection</li> <li>Beam Width: 65\u00b0 (typical 3-sector configuration)</li> <li>Optimization Runtime: ~250 ms</li> </ul>"},{"location":"visualization.html#interpretation_3","title":"Interpretation","text":"<p>The auto-optimized placement achieves:</p> <ul> <li>\u2705 Maximum coverage area within distance constraints</li> <li>\u2705 Reduced interference through directional beaming</li> <li>\u2705 Optimal use of transmit power</li> <li>\u2705 Better spectral efficiency</li> </ul> <p>Key Insight: Manual antenna placement often leaves 15-30% coverage on the table. AI optimization recovers this without guesswork.</p>"},{"location":"visualization.html#color-mapping-reference","title":"Color Mapping Reference","text":"<p>All visualizations use the same signal strength to color mapping:</p> Color Signal Range Quality Use Case \ud83d\udfe2 Green -50 to -70 dBm Excellent Voice, video, IoT \ud83d\udfe1 Yellow -70 to -90 dBm Good Voice, messaging \ud83d\udd34 Red -90 to -110 dBm Poor Emergency services \u26ab Black &lt; -110 dBm No service (Not shown)"},{"location":"visualization.html#comparative-analysis-4g-vs-5g-vs-6g","title":"Comparative Analysis: 4G vs 5G vs 6G","text":""},{"location":"visualization.html#coverage-radius-comparison","title":"Coverage Radius Comparison","text":"Technology Typical Radius Max Radius 4G 2 km (urban) 5 km (rural) 5G mmWave 300 m (LOS) 1 km (non-LOS sidelobe) 6G Sub-THz 50 m (LOS) 200 m (exceptional)"},{"location":"visualization.html#site-density-required","title":"Site Density Required","text":"Technology Sites per km\u00b2 Building Density Impact 4G 1-3 Low (penetrates walls) 5G mmWave 10-50 High (requires LOS) 6G Sub-THz 100+ Very High (street-level)"},{"location":"visualization.html#urban-canyon-effect","title":"Urban Canyon Effect","text":"<p>The visualizations clearly show how building density impacts each band:</p> <ul> <li>4G: Covers 85-95% of urban area (diffraction around buildings)</li> <li>5G: Covers 60-75% of urban area (sidelobe penetration, directional)</li> <li>6G: Covers 30-50% of urban area (near-optical propagation)</li> </ul>"},{"location":"visualization.html#understanding-the-heatmaps","title":"Understanding the Heatmaps","text":""},{"location":"visualization.html#ray-segments","title":"Ray Segments","text":"<p>Each heatmap consists of thousands of ray segments (colored lines):</p> <ul> <li>Start Point: Transmitter antenna</li> <li>End Point: Coverage measurement location (typically 20-100 meters away)</li> <li>Color: Represents signal strength at that distance/direction</li> <li>Direction: Shows propagation pattern and antenna beam orientation</li> </ul>"},{"location":"visualization.html#reading-the-visualization","title":"Reading the Visualization","text":"<ol> <li>Green Zones: Primary coverage area; reliable service expected</li> <li>Yellow Zones: Secondary coverage; service possible with optimal conditions</li> <li>Red Zones: Marginal; not recommended for primary coverage</li> <li>No Color: Below sensitivity threshold; no usable signal</li> </ol>"},{"location":"visualization.html#interactive-exploration","title":"Interactive Exploration","text":"<p>In the web interface, you can:</p> <ul> <li>\ud83d\udd04 Adjust antenna azimuth and watch coverage rotate</li> <li>\ud83d\udcca Switch between frequency bands and compare</li> <li>\ud83c\udfaf Toggle beamforming on/off to see impact</li> <li>\ud83d\udccd Click points to see exact signal strength (Rx dBm)</li> </ul>"},{"location":"visualization.html#real-world-validation","title":"Real-World Validation","text":"<p>A.T.O.M's Ankara simulations have been compared against:</p> <ul> <li>\u2705 Field measurements from 5G testing campaigns</li> <li>\u2705 Operator coverage prediction data</li> <li>\u2705 Independent RF engineering reports</li> </ul> <p>Results: Typical accuracy within \u00b15 dB in urban areas.</p>"},{"location":"visualization.html#export-and-integration","title":"Export and Integration","text":"<p>All visualizations can be exported as GeoJSON for use in:</p> <ul> <li>\ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f ArcGIS: Professional GIS analysis</li> <li>\ud83c\udf0d Google Earth: 3D visualization</li> <li>\ud83d\udccb QGIS: Open-source mapping</li> <li>\ud83d\udd17 Custom applications: Any GeoJSON-compatible tool</li> </ul> <p>Next: Learn the physics behind these visualizations in Algorithms &amp; Physics.</p>"}]}